ect marketing performance to revenue outcomes. Working at the intersection of data, strategy, and operations, you will also influence how marketing effectiveness is measured and optimized at scale. The environment is highly collaborative and intellectually demanding, requiring both technical depth and strong business intuition. This role is ideal for someone who thrives in ambiguity, enjoys solving complex problems, and wants to have a direct impact on strategic marketing decisions.\n\nAccountabilities\n\nAnalyze large and complex marketing datasets to identify trends, root causes, and performance drivers across SEM, SEO, and AI-driven acquisition channels.\nDevelop dashboards, reports, and visualization tools (e.g., Tableau) to support data-driven decision-making across marketing leadership.\nBuild forecasting models, perform statistical analysis, and run experiments to evaluate marketing performance and optimize spend allocation.\nDefine and standardize marketing metrics that accurately reflect business objectives and align cross-functional teams.\nTranslate data insights into clear, actionable recommendations that improve conversion, efficiency, and revenue generation.\nMap end-to-end marketing funnels and data flows from acquisition through revenue generation to improve visibility and optimization opportunities.\nLeverage generative AI tools to enhance analytics workflows, automate reporting, and assess AI-driven search channel performance.\nCollaborate closely with marketing, data, and business stakeholders to align priorities and support strategic initiatives.\n\nRequirements\n\nBachelor\u2019s degree in a quantitative or analytical field such as Mathematics, Statistics, Finance, Engineering, or Economics.\n5+ years of experience in data analytics, business intelligence, or marketing analytics roles.\nAt least 2+ years of experience in consulting or analytical operations environments.\nStrong expertise in analyzing SEM, SEO, and AI-driven or generative search 