d escalated consumer inquiries by utilizing <strong>CRM telemetry</strong> and historical performance metrics, accelerating ticket resolution speed by 35% across high-volume queues.</li>\n    <li>Analyzed user interaction trends to identify recurring <strong>service bottlenecks</strong>, partnering with operations leads to streamline workflows and boost customer satisfaction.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Founder | Creative Director, Maerke Stratcomm \u2013 New Delhi, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>June 2010 \u2013 July 2020</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Directed <strong>commercial analytics</strong>, pricing strategy, and market segmentation for 15+ B2B and retail clients, driving a 30% increase in customer acquisition.</li>\n    <li>Implemented <strong>funnel performance tracking</strong> and ROI attribution models across regional distribution channels, expanding HORECA and enterprise account revenue by 25%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>", "exp2_bullets": "", "exp3_bullets": ""}, "clHtml": "<p class=\"salutation\">Dear Hiring Manager at Jobgether,</p>\n<p>I am writing to apply for the Senior Marketing Analyst, Strategy & Analytics role at Jobgether. With over five years of hands-on experience building reliable SQL and Python reporting pipelines, designing executive Tableau dashboards, and partnering with product and operations leaders, I am eager to contribute immediately to Jobgether's data and analytics goals.</p>\n<p>Throughout my career across high-volume operational and business intelligence environments, I have focused on turning complex, fragmented datasets into clear, trustworthy decision frameworks. Whether automating recurring ETL workflows or establishing governed KPI definitions across teams, I prioritize data accuracy and practical business impact.</p>\n<p>In my recent work, I re-engineered manual reporting workflows into automated SQL and Tableau pipelines that reduced reporting latency by over 40% while uncovering key drivers of funnel conversion and SLA performance. This blend of technical execution and stakeholder communication aligns closely with what Jobgether seeks in this position.</p>\n<p>I thrive in fast-paced environments where requirements evolve quickly and cross-functional clarity is essential. My background spans end-to-end requirement gathering, UAT governance, root-cause diagnostics, and translating technical findings for non-technical leadership.</p>\n<p>Thank you for your time and consideration. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my background in SQL, Python, Tableau, and business analysis can support Jobgether's upcoming initiatives.</p>"}, {"sNo": "2", "sNoNum": 2, "resumeId": "08b67f41-ffe6-443a-985f-52a83db6244e", "company": "Orange Business", "industry": "Telecommunications & Digital Integration", "jobId": "N/A", "title": "Senior Business Analyst", "jd": "About the job\nAbout Us\n\nJoin us at Orange Business!\n\nWe are a network and digital integrator that understands the entire value chain of the digital world, freeing our customers to focus on the strategic initiatives that shape their business.\n\nEvery day, you will collaborate with a team dedicated to providing consistent, sustainable global solutions, no matter where our customers operate. With over 30,000 employees across Asia, the Americas, Africa, and Europe, we offer a dynamic environment to develop and perfect your skills in a field filled with exciting challenges and opportunities.\n\nAbout The Role\n\nThe International zone is comprised of four regions with various capabilities supporting the digital transformation of MNC customers.\n\nEach region defines its own strategic plans, rolling up to the International strategy, highlighting their focus on e.g. segments, verticals, partnerships, etc\u2026\n\nThe Senior Business Analyst role is instrumental to support and drive the international business (with the regions and the marketing teams).\n\nInterpreting the market intelligence to be able to lead the identification of key target regions/ segments/ verticals.\n\nThese market insights will be instrumental to boost commercial activity, target new customers and grow existing customers.\n\nWhile the overall marketing activity and commercial lead is managed by the Regional teams, a proactive approach will help us to push & influence our business.\n\nMission\n\nAs Senior Business Analyst you will manage the market insights activities for OBI and support the international regions with market insights.\n\nMain activities\n\n Become Market Intelligence savy! Study market intelligence to be able to identify, recommend and challenge the regions on segment/ vertical strategic focus \n Engage with International Sales & Marketing to define insights & recommendation to support our revenue and GM ambition (grow, keep, expand...), marketing by vertical, revenue by vertical, which accts? which new logos? look at TML.... \n Facilitate consumption of market intelligence data: inspire and teach the OBI Sales & Marketing team \n Share and present data insights to a larger OBI audience (in the future) and act as the senior data expert for OBI \n Contribute to the strategy/planning process by providing market data \n\nResponsibilities\n\n About you \n\nMarket Intelligence vs Marketing\n\n Marketing campaigns are centrally managed by Marketing teams \n Market insights requests are documented and scoped by Marketing teams \n Market insights are provided and shared by Market Intelligence \n Market intelligence is not in charge of the Marketing plan, Budget plan or Strategic Plan. However, Market Intelligence should have an understanding of these plans, with a clear demand to come with proactive insights where relevant \n Delivery of market studies, market targeting, or campaign input is done by Market intelligence and delivered to the (regional) Marketing SPOC \n The target process includes the need to document each campaign in the CRM, allowing us to trace follow-up and commercial performance \n\nMarket Intelligence vs Business Intelligence\n\n Market intelligence applies market data to provide marketing recommendations, this is done for prospects or customers, \n Business intelligence provides commercial reporting, order tracking and revenue reporting \n Marketing Intelligence will rely on customer data provided by the BI team (Customer Base Mngt, commercial performance, order tracking\u2026) \n\nKey Knowledge and Abilities:\n\n understanding of Orange Business strategy and solutions/portfolio \n understanding of International customers and its business buildup \n understanding market & sales intelligence and facilitate embedding this in the Marketing plan \n ability to animate the main users of the market data intelligence \n\nKey Skills: \n\nMandatory skills: \n\n Proven proficiency in Data Analytics (using preferably Tableau but other BI tools are acceptable - Tableau, QlikSense/QlikView, Looker, etc.) \n Proficiency in data modelling & automation (ETL, ELT, creating & maintaining data pipelines) \n Data Science/ML Engineering background - understanding statistical models & implementing suitable ML models for different UCs (supervised vs unsupervised modelling), programming language - preferably Python (pandas, numpy, scikit-learn, etc.) \n Proficiency in Business analytics -> full E2E delivery \n Solid stakeholder & project management skills \n\nOptional Skills\n\n Agile frameworks (SAFe, LEAN, etc.) \n Knowledge of Scrum/Kanban \n Knowledge of CI/CD best practices (GIT - GitLab, Sourcetree, etc.) \n CRM systems (SFDC is preferred but understanding CRM data governance is a plus) \n\nBase salary from 2 410 \u20ac brutto per month, actual salary is likely to be higher based on skills, knowledge and experience.\n\nYou bring rigor, passion for challenges, and determination. You seek the opportunity to expand your expertise, achieve your goals, and thrive.",