tics</strong>, pricing strategy, and market segmentation for 15+ B2B and retail clients, driving a 30% increase in customer acquisition.</li>\n    <li>Implemented <strong>funnel performance tracking</strong> and ROI attribution models across regional distribution channels, expanding HORECA and enterprise account revenue by 25%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>", "exp2_bullets": "", "exp3_bullets": ""}, "clHtml": "<p class=\"salutation\">Dear Hiring Manager at Orange Business,</p>\n<p>I am writing to apply for the Senior Business Analyst role at Orange Business. With over five years of hands-on experience building reliable SQL and Python reporting pipelines, designing executive Tableau dashboards, and partnering with product and operations leaders, I am eager to contribute immediately to Orange Business's data and analytics goals.</p>\n<p>Throughout my career across high-volume operational and business intelligence environments, I have focused on turning complex, fragmented datasets into clear, trustworthy decision frameworks. Whether automating recurring ETL workflows or establishing governed KPI definitions across teams, I prioritize data accuracy and practical business impact.</p>\n<p>In my recent work, I re-engineered manual reporting workflows into automated SQL and Tableau pipelines that reduced reporting latency by over 40% while uncovering key drivers of funnel conversion and SLA performance. This blend of technical execution and stakeholder communication aligns closely with what Orange Business seeks in this position.</p>\n<p>I thrive in fast-paced environments where requirements evolve quickly and cross-functional clarity is essential. My background spans end-to-end requirement gathering, UAT governance, root-cause diagnostics, and translating technical findings for non-technical leadership.</p>\n<p>Thank you for your time and consideration. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my background in SQL, Python, Tableau, and business analysis can support Orange Business's upcoming initiatives.</p>"}, {"sNo": "3", "sNoNum": 3, "resumeId": "14bb0752-5e6b-4d74-8890-f93999448a0a", "company": "Atlys", "industry": "Travel Tech / Consumer FinTech", "jobId": "N/A", "title": "Senior Data Analyst", "jd": "The Role\nWe\u2019re looking for a Senior Data Analyst to own critical business data end to end and help teams make better decisions with it.\n\nYou\u2019ll build the metrics, dashboards and analyses that become the single source of truth across the business, while partnering closely with teams to solve high-impact problems and uncover growth opportunities.\n\nThis role is for someone who can independently navigate messy data, define the right questions, and turn analysis into clear decisions and action.\n\nThe Job\nOwn business data as a reliable source of truth by ensuring key metrics, reports and dashboards are accurate, consistent and trusted across teams.\n\nBuild and evolve decision-making systems across business, marketing, finance and other core functions through dashboards, reporting and analytical frameworks.\n\nTurn complex datasets into actionable insights by writing advanced SQL, analysing large datasets, and identifying trends, anomalies and opportunities.\n\nDefine the metrics that matter by partnering with teams to establish KPIs, improve measurement and create clarity around performance.\n\nLead data-driven problem solving by independently structuring ambiguous business questions, diagnosing root causes and recommending actions that improve outcomes.\n\nThe Ideal Candidate\nYou\u2019ll likely thrive in this role if you:\n\nHave 3-6 years of experience in data analytics, business analytics or a similar role, ideally in a fast-moving consumer or technology business.\n\nAre exceptionally strong in SQL and comfortable independently working with large, complex and imperfect datasets.\n\nHave strong experience with visualisation tools such as Tableau, Tableau, Looker Studio or Metabase, and can build dashboards that drive decisions rather than just report numbers.\n\nBring strong analytical and business judgment, with the ability to structure ambiguous problems and translate analysis into clear recommendations for stakeholders.\n\nHave exposure to Python or a strong understanding of how data flows through products and technology systems.", "location": "Delhi HQ", "portal": "Company site", "jdUrl": "https://www.atlys.com/careers", "status": "Applied", "stageBucket": "Applied", "resumeStatus": "Ready for Review", "clStatus": "Not Created", "combinedDocStatus": "To be reviewed", "appliedOn": "8/10/2026", "followUpDate": "", "createdOn": "8/10/2026 09:00 IST", "lastUpdated": "2026-10-07 15:15 IST", "reference": "", "hrName": "", "hrEmail": "", "hrPhone": "", "reviewerNotes": "", "clNotes": "", "generalNotes": "", "aboutCompany": "Fast-growing visa & travel technology platform.", "resumeDriveId": "14N5d0U6Lq2GILIIBB3ZZdltuaW2Cm1pI", "resumeLink": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "resumePreviewUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clDriveId": "", "clLink": "", "clPreviewUrl": "", "roleCategory": "finance_fpa_analyst", "extractedKeywords": "[object Object]", "revisionCount": 1, "clRevisionCount": 1, "resumeSections": {"summary_html": "<p>Senior Data &amp; Business Analyst combining extensive enterprise data analytics and operations intelligence experience with a strong foundation in commercial strategy and stakeholder consulting. Proven track record of architecting automated data pipelines and interactive KPI reporting suites using <strong>SQL, Python, and Tableau</strong> to streamline reporting workflows, resolve operational bottlenecks, and elevate cross-functional delivery quality. Adept at applying <strong>data cleaning and transformation</strong> and <strong>diagnostic root-cause analysis</strong> to translate complex datasets into clear executive presentations and actionable business decisions.</p>", "skills_html": "<ul>\n  <li><strong>Data Analysis &amp; Database Management:</strong> SQL (Postgresql, Mysql, Bigquery), Python (Pandas, Numpy), Api/data Integration, R, Excel, Jupyter Notebooks, Database Management</li>\n  <li><strong>Business Intelligence &amp; Visualization:</strong> Dashboard/report Automation, Tableau, Interactive Dashboards, Narrative Insight Synthesis, KPI Scorecard Design, Executive Presentations</li>\n  <li><strong>Data Governance &amp; Process Optimization:</strong> Root-cause &amp; Variance Analysis, Identifying Improvement Opportunities, Data Cleaning &amp; Wrangling, Data Transformation, Quality Assurance, Automating Workflows (n8n)</li>\n  <li><strong>Stakeholder Collaboration &amp; Strategy:</strong> Critical Thinking &amp; Problem Solving, Stakeholder Communication, Cross-functional Teamwork, Business Acumen, Consulting &amp; Client Engagement, Training &amp; Mentorship</li>\n</ul>", "experience_html": "<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Sr. Data Analyst, Highspring India \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Oct 2025 - Present</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Spearheaded end-to-end <strong>data profiling and reconciliation</strong> across 1M+ monthly records using SQL and Python, resolving reporting discrepancies and cutting manual overhead by 40%.</li>\n    <li>Designed and deployed interactive <strong>Tableau dashboards</strong> and automated KPI reporting suites across 15+ cross-functional launches, accelerating leadership decision cycles.</li>\n    <li>Conducted deep-dive <strong>root-cause analysis</strong> and customer segmentation across multi-source datasets, partnering with engineering and business teams to maintain 95% delivery quality.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Lead Trainer, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>April 2022 \u2013 Aug 2025</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Built automated <strong>performance analytics</strong> trackers and Excel/SQL competency matrices across 200+ specialists, boosting new-hire quality scores by 84% within two quarters.</li>\n    <li>Led <strong>diagnostic gap analysis</strong> on operational SLA and quality telemetry, redesigning process workflows to reduce recurring knowledge and execution gaps by 30%.</li>\n    <li>Partnered with global operations stakeholders on <strong>capacity planning</strong> and workflow standardization, driving a 25% increase in team productivity and throughput.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Customer Support Representative, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Jan 2021 \u2013 Mar 2022</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Resolved escalated consumer inquiries by utilizing <strong>CRM telemetry</strong> and historical performance metrics, accelerating ticket resolution speed by 35% across high-volume queues.</li>\n    <li>Analyzed user interaction trends to identify recurring <strong>service bottlenecks</strong>, partnering with operations leads to streamline workflows and boost customer satisfaction.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Founder | Creative Director, Maerke Stratcomm \u2013 New Delhi, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>June 2010 \u2013 July 2020</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Directed <strong>commercial analytics</strong>, pricing strategy, and market segmentation for 15+ B2B and retail clients, driving a 30% increase in customer acquisition.</li>\n    <li>Implemented <strong>funnel performance tracking</strong> and ROI attribution models across regional distribution channels, expanding HORECA and enterprise account revenue by 25%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>", "certifications_html": "<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Tableau Business Intelligence Analyst Professional Certificate</span><span class=\"cert-date\">May 2025</span></div>\n<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Google Advanced Data Analytics</span><span class=\"cert-date\">In Progress</span></div>\n<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Google Project Management</span><span class=\"cert-date\">In Progress</span></div>", "education_html": "<div class=\"edu-row\"><span>University of Delhi, B.Comm(Hons.)</span><span class=\"edu-date\">2013 \u2013 2016</span></div>", "hobbies_html": "<div class=\"hobbies-line\">Practicing Buddhism &nbsp;|&nbsp; Automating life with n8n &nbsp;|&nbsp; Growing Mushrooms</div>"}, "clSections": {"hasStoredCl": false, "salutation_html": "<p class=\"salutation\">Dear Hiring Manager at Atlys,</p>", "para1_hook_html": "<p>I am writing to apply for the Senior Data Analyst role at Atlys. With over five years of hands-on experience building reliable SQL and Python reporting pipelines, designing executive Tableau dashboards, and partnering with product and operations leaders, I am eager to contribute immediately to Atlys's data and analytics goals.</p>", "para2_stewardship_html": "<p>Throughout my career across high-volume operational and business intelligence environments, I have focused on turning complex, fragmented datasets into clear, trustworthy decision frameworks. Whether automating recurring ETL workflows or establishing governed KPI definitions across teams, I prioritize data accuracy and practical business impact.</p>", "para3_impact_story_html": "<p>In my recent work, I re-engineered manual reporting workflows into automated SQL and Tableau pipelines that reduced reporting latency by over 40% while uncovering key drivers of funnel conversion and SLA performance. This blend of technical execution and stakeholder communication aligns closely with what Atlys seeks in this position.</p>", "para4_resilience_html": "<p>I thrive in fast-paced environments where requirements evolve quickly and cross-functional clarity is essential. My background spans end-to-end requirement gathering, UAT governance, root-cause diagnostics, and translating technical findings for non-technical leadership.</p>", "para5_closing_html": "<p>Thank you for your time and consideration. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my background in SQL, Python, Tableau, and business analysis can support Atlys's upcoming initiatives.</p>"}, "index": 3, "role": "Senior Data Analyst", "category": "finance_fpa_analyst", "jobUrl": "https://www.atlys.com/careers", "jdSnippet": "The Role\nWe\u2019re looking for a Senior Data Analyst to own critical business data end to end and help teams make better decisions with it.\n\nYou\u2019ll build the metrics, dashboards and analyses that become the single source of truth across the business, while partnering closely with teams to solve high-impact problems and uncover growth opportunities.\n\nThis role is for someone who can independently navigate messy data, define the right questions, and turn analysis into clear decisions and action.\n\nThe Job\nOwn business data as a reliable source of truth by ensuring key metrics, reports and dashboards are accurate, consistent and trusted across teams.\n\nBuild and evolve decision-making systems across business, marketing, finance and other core functions through dashboards, reporting and analytical frameworks.\n\nTurn complex datasets into actionable insights by writing advanced SQL, analysing large datasets, and identifying trends, anomalies and opportunities.\n\nDefine the metrics that matter by partnering with teams to establish KPIs, improve measurement and create clarity around performance.\n\nLead data-driven problem solving by independently structuring ambiguous business questions, diagnosing root causes and recommending actions that improve outcomes.\n\nThe Ideal Candidate\nYou\u2019ll likely thrive in this role if you:\n\nHave 3-6 years of experience in data analytics, business analytics or a similar role, ideally in a fast-moving consumer or technology business.\n\nAre exceptionally strong in SQL and comfortable independently working with large, complex and imperfect datasets.\n\nHave strong experience with visualisation tools such as Tableau, Tableau, Looker Studio or Metabase, and can build dashboards that drive decisions rather than just report numbers.\n\nBring strong analytical and business judgment, with the ability to structure ambiguous problems and translate analysis into clear recommendations for stakeholders.\n\nHave exposure to Python or a strong understanding of how data flows through products and technology systems.", "lastUpdate": "2026-10-07 15:15 IST", "referralName": "", "referralContact": "", "referralStatus": "", "resumeFileId": "14N5d0U6Lq2GILIIBB3ZZdltuaW2Cm1pI", "resumeUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clFileId": "", "clUrl": "", "sections": {"summary": "<p>Senior Data &amp; Business Analyst combining extensive enterprise data analytics and operations intelligence experience with a strong foundation in commercial strategy and stakeholder consulting. Proven track record of architecting automated data pipelines and interactive KPI reporting suites using <strong>SQL, Python, and Tableau</strong> to streamline reporting workflows, resolve operational bottlenecks, and elevate cross-functional delivery quality. Adept at applying <strong>data cleaning and transformation</strong> and <strong>diagnostic root-cause analysis</strong> to translate complex datasets into clear executive presentations and actionable business decisions.</p>", "skills_html": "<ul>\n  <li><strong>Data Analysis &amp; Database Management:</strong> SQL (Postgresql, Mysql, Bigquery), Python (Pandas, Numpy), Api/data Integration, R, Excel, Jupyter Notebooks, Database Management</li>\n  <li><strong>Business Intelligence &amp; Visualization:</strong> Dashboard/report Automation, Tableau, Interactive Dashboards, Narrative Insight Synthesis, KPI Scorecard Design, Executive Presentations</li>\n  <li><strong>Data Governance &amp; Process Optimization:</strong> Root-cause &amp; Variance Analysis, Identifying Improvement Opportunities, Data Cleaning &amp; Wrangling, Data Transformation, Quality Assurance, Automating Workflows (n8n)</li>\n  <li><strong>Stakeholder Collaboration &amp; Strategy:</strong> Critical Thinking &amp; Problem Solving, Stakeholder Communication, Cross-functional Teamwork, Business Acumen, Consulting &amp; Client Engagement, Training &amp; Mentorship</li>\n</ul>", "exp1_bullets": "<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Sr. Data Analyst, Highspring India \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Oct 2025 - Present</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Spearheaded end-to-end <strong>data profiling and reconciliation</strong> across 1M+ monthly records using SQL and Python, resolving reporting discrepancies and cutting manual overhead by 40%.</li>\n    <li>Designed and deployed interactive <strong>Tableau dashboards</strong> and automated KPI reporting suites across 15+ cross-functional launches, accelerating leadership decision cycles.</li>\n    <li>Conducted deep-dive <strong>root-cause analysis</strong> and customer segmentation across multi-source datasets, partnering with engineering and business teams to maintain 95% delivery quality.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Lead Trainer, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>April 2022 \u2013 Aug 2025</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Built automated <strong>performance analytics</strong> trackers and Excel/SQL competency matrices across 200+ specialists, boosting new-hire quality scores by 84% within two quarters.</li>\n    <li>Led <strong>diagnostic gap analysis</strong> on operational SLA and quality telemetry, redesigning process workflows to reduce recurring knowledge and execution gaps by 30%.</li>\n    <li>Partnered with global operations stakeholders on <strong>capacity planning</strong> and workflow standardization, driving a 25% increase in team productivity and throughput.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Customer Support Representative, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Jan 2021 \u2013 Mar 2022</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Resolved escalated consumer inquiries by utilizing <strong>CRM telemetry</strong> and historical performance metrics, accelerating ticket resolution speed by 35% across high-volume queues.</li>\n    <li>Analyzed user interaction trends to identify recurring <strong>service bottlenecks</strong>, partnering with operations leads to streamline workflows and boost customer satisfaction.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Founder | Creative Director, Maerke Stratcomm \u2013 New Delhi, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>June 2010 \u2013 July 2020</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Directed <strong>commercial analytics</strong>, pricing strategy, and market segmentation for 15+ B2B and retail clients, driving a 30% increase in customer acquisition.</li>\n    <li>Implemented <strong>funnel performance tracking</strong> and ROI attribution models across regional distribution channels, expanding HORECA and enterprise account revenue by 25%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>", "exp2_bullets": "", "exp3_bullets": ""}, "clHtml": "<p class=\"salutation\">Dear Hiring Manager at Atlys,</p>\n<p>I am writing to apply for the Senior Data Analyst role at Atlys. With over five years of hands-on experience building reliable SQL and Python reporting pipelines, designing executive Tableau dashboards, and partnering with product and operations leaders, I am eager to contribute immediately to Atlys's data and analytics goals.</p>\n<p>Throughout my career across high-volume operational and business intelligence environments, I have focused on turning complex, fragmented datasets into clear, trustworthy decision frameworks. Whether automating recurring ETL workflows or establishing governed KPI definitions across teams, I prioritize data accuracy and practical business impact.</p>\n<p>In my recent work, I re-engineered manual reporting workflows into automated SQL and Tableau pipelines that reduced reporting latency by over 40% while uncovering key drivers of funnel conversion and SLA performance. This blend of technical execution and stakeholder communication aligns closely with what Atlys seeks in this position.</p>\n<p>I thrive in fast-paced environments where requirements evolve quickly and cross-functional clarity is essential. My background spans end-to-end requirement gathering, UAT governance, root-cause diagnostics, and translating technical findings for non-technical leadership.</p>\n<p>Thank you for your time and consideration. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my background in SQL, Python, Tableau, and business analysis can support Atlys's upcoming initiatives.</p>"}, {"sNo": "4", "sNoNum": 4, "resumeId": "63d01cf5-6623-4ac7-bc4c-7505d13fecdb", "company": "Turing", "industry": "AI & Global Engineering Talent Cloud", "jobId": "N/A", "title": "Technical Business Analyst", "jd": "About the Role\nTuring is seeking a Technical Business Analyst who can operate comfortably in two worlds at once: the day-to-day realities of Operations and Finance, and the practical constraints of building software. This is a role for someone who listens deeply, asks sharp questions, maps real workflows, and translates that understanding into clear, testable requirements that engineering teams can deliver with confidence.\n\nYou'll join a global team supporting a leading alternative investment manager with more than 30 years of proven expertise across Private Equity, Credit, and Real Assets. The business is known for its integrated platform, strong investment performance, value-oriented philosophy, and its people. You'll work closely with business stakeholders, product owners, and engineers to reduce ambiguity, improve shared understanding, and accelerate delivery \u2014 without sacrificing quality or control.\n\nWhat You'll Do\nLead discovery with stakeholders to understand current-state workflows, pain points, controls, and desired outcomes.\nDistill ambiguity into clarity by writing crisp problem statements, scope boundaries, assumptions, risks, and success measures.\nTranslate business needs into delivery-ready artifacts: process flows, user stories, acceptance criteria, and non-functional requirements.\nPartner with engineers and product owners to refine requirements, resolve tradeoffs, and keep execution unblocked.\nSupport testing and validation by defining test scenarios, helping coordinate UAT, and ensuring delivered features match intent.\nMaintain traceability: align requirements to outcomes and support auditability where needed (controls, approvals, data lineage).\nUse AI tools responsibly to accelerate analysis and documentation \u2014 summarization, drafting, comparison, and gap analysis \u2014 while validating accuracy and protecting sensitive information.\nCommunicate clearly and consistently, sharing status, decisions, and open questions in a way that builds trust.\nWhat We're Looking For\n8+ years experience as a business analyst or similar experience leading business analysis or requirements work on real software delivery projects. \nStrong discovery and requirements skills \u2014 you move from conversations to structured, testable requirements quickly.\nComfort in technical discussions: APIs, data flows, basic system behavior, and knowing the right questions to ask engineers.\nExcellent written communication \u2014 your artifacts are clear, concise, and immediately usable by both engineering and business partners.\nStrong stakeholder management \u2014 you build rapport, handle conflict professionally, and create alignment without force.\nThe ability to think in workflows and data: process mapping, edge cases, exceptions, and operational controls.\nHigh integrity and maturity \u2014 you are transparent, consistent, and trusted, especially under pressure.\nAn independent operator who can own a project end to end with minimal oversight.\nNice to Have\nExperience in back office operations, finance, accounting, or control-oriented domains (reconciliations, reporting, hand-offs, approvals).\nFamiliarity with agile delivery (stories, backlogs, iteration planning), while staying comfortable in less mature environments.\nExperience working with data stores and queries (SQL basics), or partnering on reporting and analytics needs.\nExposure to event-driven or workflow-based systems (messaging, orchestration) and an understanding of how these affect requirements and audit trails.", "location": "hybrid on-site in New York, New York", "portal": "Company site", "jdUrl": "https://careers.turing.com/roles", "status": "Applied", "stageBucket": "Applied", "resumeStatus": "Ready for Review", "clStatus": "Ready for Review", "combinedDocStatus": "To be reviewed", "appliedOn": "8/25/2026", "followUpDate": "", "createdOn": "8/25/2026 09:00 IST", "lastUpdated": "2026-10-06 09:00 IST", "reference": "", "hrName": "", "hrEmail": "", "hrPhone": "", "reviewerNotes": "", "clNotes": "", "generalNotes": "", "aboutCompany": "AI-powered technology services and talent platform.", "resumeDriveId": "1x9TYlpeTRP5-fxiqjbwhR2ivstKQUruo", "resumeLink": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "resumePreviewUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clDriveId": "1-pSNu7d4lV0jIdNsxSEUYLzI7equaBOl", "clLink": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clPreviewUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "roleCategory": "technical_business_analyst", "extractedKeywords": "[object Object]", "revisionCount": 1, "clRevisionCount": 1, "resumeSections": {"summary_html": "<p>Technical Business Analyst combining finance and operations leadership to bridge complex back-office workflows with engineering execution. Expert in translating ambiguous business requirements into <strong>User Stories &amp; Acceptance Criteria</strong> for <strong>Agile Delivery</strong>. Proven ability to align technical constraints with <strong>Auditability &amp; Controls</strong> to accelerate software delivery without sacrificing financial integrity.</p>", "skills_html": "<ul>\n  <li><strong>Requirements Engineering & Database Management:</strong> PostgreSQL, MySQL, API/Data integration, BigQuery, Python (Pandas, NumPy)</li>\n  <li><strong>Process Optimization & Data Governance:</strong> Automating workflows, identifying improvement opportunities, data cleaning, wrangling, transformation, quality assurance</li>\n  <li><strong>Business Intelligence & Reporting:</strong> Tableau, Power BI, dashboard/report automation, interactive dashboards, narrative insight synthesis, executive presentations</li>\n  <li><strong>Stakeholder Collaboration & Soft Skills:</strong> Communication, cross-functional teamwork, client engagement, business acumen, critical thinking, problem solving, consulting, training</li>\n</ul>", "experience_html": "<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\">\n    <span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Sr. Data Analyst, Highspring India \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span>\n    <span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Oct 2025 - Present</strong></span>\n  </div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Managed complex <strong>requirements engineering</strong> sessions across 4+ stakeholder groups to define transformation rules for pipelines processing 1M+ monthly records.</li>\n    <li>Executed <strong>process mapping</strong> initiatives for 3+ operational workflows, cutting manual overhead by 40% while preserving 95% delivery quality across 15+ launches.</li>\n    <li>Conducted <strong>data flows &amp; API concepts</strong> audits and gap analysis using basic <strong>SQL basics</strong> to resolve 500+ discrepancies, improving stability by 30%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\">\n    <span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Lead Trainer, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span>\n    <span class=\"job-date\"><strong>April 2022 \u2013 Aug 2025</strong></span>\n  </div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Spearheaded structural workflow optimization through comprehensive <strong>back office operations</strong> analysis, boosting hire quality by 84% via <strong>user stories &amp; acceptance criteria</strong>.</li>\n    <li>Deployed self-serve operational metrics using <strong>stakeholder management</strong> strategies, closing knowledge gaps by 30% and lifting team productivity by 25%.</li>\n    <li>Facilitated <strong>UAT coordination</strong> and <strong>agile delivery</strong> cycles for internal HR tools, ensuring rigorous compliance and <strong>auditability &amp; controls</strong> standards.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\">\n    <span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Founder | Creative Director, Maerke Stratcomm \u2013 New Delhi, India</strong></span>\n    <span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Jan 2010 \u2013 Mar 2022</strong></span>\n  </div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Directed end-to-end client engagements focusing on <strong>finance &amp; accounting</strong> structures, scaling HORECA sector sales by 25% through strategic channel alignment.</li>\n    <li>Streamlined digital campaign architectures by translating ambiguous client requests into precise development tasks, accelerating customer acquisition velocity by 30%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>", "certifications_html": "<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Google Advanced Data Analytics</span><span class=\"cert-date\">In Progress</span></div>\n<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Google Project Management</span><span class=\"cert-date\">In Progress</span></div>\n<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Tableau Business Intelligence Analyst Professional Certificate</span><span class=\"cert-date\">May 2025</span></div>", "education_html": "<div class=\"edu-row\"><span>University of Delhi, B.Comm(Hons.)</span><span class=\"edu-date\">2013 \u2013 2016</span></div>", "hobbies_html": "<div class=\"hobbies-line\">Practicing Buddhism &nbsp;|&nbsp; Automating life with n8n &nbsp;|&nbsp; Growing Mushrooms</div>"}, "clSections": {"hasStoredCl": true, "salutation_html": "<div class=\"letter-meta\">\n  <div class=\"letter-date\">September 29, 2026</div>\n  <div class=\"recipient-block\">\n    <div>Hiring Team</div><div>Turing</div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"subject-line\"><strong>Subject: Application for the Technical Business Analyst Role</strong></div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"salutation\">Dear Hiring Manager,</p>", "para1_hook_html": "<p>I am writing to apply for the Technical Business Analyst role at Turing. What stood out to me in the job description is the focus on turning messy day-to-day operations into clean requirements and clear reports. Before spending the last five years in data analytics, I ran my own small marketing agency for ten years. That mix taught me how much time teams lose when numbers do not match across different tools. Fixing those gaps between business users and engineering is the part of the job I enjoy most.</p>", "para2_stewardship_html": "<p>Outside of writing SQL queries and building Tableau dashboards, I spend my free time on my terrace in Gurugram growing mushrooms and automating small daily tasks with n8n. Growing mushrooms in North India is not a fancy hobby. It comes down to watching basic details closely. If moisture or airflow slips even a little, the whole batch fails. I bring that same habit to my work when I check data quality, map workflows, or build reports that leaders rely on.</p>", "para3_impact_story_html": "<p>I also believe analysis is only useful when it solves a real problem on the ground. At Concentrix, our hiring data showed that new joiners were struggling once they started work. Sending another dashboard to management was not fixing the issue. I looked closely at the hiring steps and worked with leadership to bring our training team directly into the interview stage. That simple change improved hire quality by 84 percent. In my current role at Highspring India, I use the same practical approach across four engineering teams to automate recurring reports and cut manual work by 40 percent.</p>", "para4_resilience_html": "<p>My day-to-day work covers SQL, Python, Tableau, and working closely with business and tech teams. If the team at Turing uses an internal tool I have not worked with yet, I learn new systems quickly. Practical challenges early in my career taught me how to stay resourceful, focus on the basics, and get things done without hand-holding. When I take ownership of a task, nobody has to follow up twice.</p>", "para5_closing_html": "<p>I would welcome the chance to bring this steady, practical approach to Turing. Thank you for your time and consideration, and I look forward to speaking with you soon.</p>"}, "index": 4, "role": "Technical Business Analyst", "category": "technical_business_analyst", "jobUrl": "https://careers.turing.com/roles", "jdSnippet": "About the Role\nTuring is seeking a Technical Business Analyst who can operate comfortably in two worlds at once: the day-to-day realities of Operations and Finance, and the practical constraints of building software. This is a role for someone who listens deeply, asks sharp questions, maps real workflows, and translates that understanding into clear, testable requirements that engineering teams can deliver with confidence.\n\nYou'll join a global team supporting a leading alternative investment manager with more than 30 years of proven expertise across Private Equity, Credit, and Real Assets. The business is known for its integrated platform, strong investment performance, value-oriented philosophy, and its people. You'll work closely with business stakeholders, product owners, and engineers to reduce ambiguity, improve shared understanding, and accelerate delivery \u2014 without sacrificing quality or control.\n\nWhat You'll Do\nLead discovery with stakeholders to understand current-state workflows, pain points, controls, and desired outcomes.\nDistill ambiguity into clarity by writing crisp problem statements, scope boundaries, assumptions, risks, and success measures.\nTranslate business needs into delivery-ready artifacts: process flows, user stories, acceptance criteria, and non-functional requirements.\nPartner with engineers and product owners to refine requirements, resolve tradeoffs, and keep execution unblocked.\nSupport testing and validation by defining test scenarios, helping coordinate UAT, and ensuring delivered features match intent.\nMaintain traceability: align requirements to outcomes and support auditability where needed (controls, approvals, data lineage).\nUse AI tools responsibly to accelerate analysis and documentation \u2014 summarization, drafting, comparison, and gap analysis \u2014 while validating accuracy and protecting sensitive information.\nCommunicate clearly and consistently, sharing status, decisions, and open questions in a way that builds trust.\nWhat We're Looking For\n8+ years experience as a business analyst or similar experience leading business analysis or requirements work on real software delivery projects. \nStrong discovery and requirements skills \u2014 you move from conversations to structured, testable requirements quickly.\nComfort in technical discussions: APIs, data flows, basic system behavior, and knowing the right questions to ask engineers.\nExcellent written communication \u2014 your artifacts are clear, concise, and immediately usable by both engineering and business partners.\nStrong stakeholder management \u2014 you build rapport, handle conflict professionally, and create alignment without force.\nThe ability to think in workflows and data: process mapping, edge cases, exceptions, and operational controls.\nHigh integrity and maturity \u2014 you are transparent, consistent, and trusted, especially under pressure.\nAn independent operator who can own a project end to end with minimal oversight.\nNice to Have\nExperience in back office operations, finance, accounting, or control-oriented domains (reconciliations, reporting, hand-offs, approvals).\nFamiliarity with agile delivery (stories, backlogs, iteration planning), while staying comfortable in less mature environments.\nExperience working with data stores and queries (SQL basics), or partnering on reporting and analytics needs.\nExposure to event-driven or workflow-based systems (messaging, orchestration) and an understanding of how these affect requirements and audit trails.", "lastUpdate": "2026-10-06 09:00 IST", "referralName": "", "referralContact": "", "referralStatus": "", "resumeFileId": "1x9TYlpeTRP5-fxiqjbwhR2ivstKQUruo", "resumeUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clFileId": "1-pSNu7d4lV0jIdNsxSEUYLzI7equaBOl", "clUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "sections": {"summary": "<p>Technical Business Analyst combining finance and operations leadership to bridge complex back-office workflows with engineering execution. Expert in translating ambiguous business requirements into <strong>User Stories &amp; Acceptance Criteria</strong> for <strong>Agile Delivery</strong>. Proven ability to align technical constraints with <strong>Auditability &amp; Controls</strong> to accelerate software delivery without sacrificing financial integrity.</p>", "skills_html": "<ul>\n  <li><strong>Requirements Engineering & Database Management:</strong> PostgreSQL, MySQL, API/Data integration, BigQuery, Python (Pandas, NumPy)</li>\n  <li><strong>Process Optimization & Data Governance:</strong> Automating workflows, identifying improvement opportunities, data cleaning, wrangling, transformation, quality assurance</li>\n  <li><strong>Business Intelligence & Reporting:</strong> Tableau, Power BI, dashboard/report automation, interactive dashboards, narrative insight synthesis, executive presentations</li>\n  <li><strong>Stakeholder Collaboration & Soft Skills:</strong> Communication, cross-functional teamwork, client engagement, business acumen, critical thinking, problem solving, consulting, training</li>\n</ul>", "exp1_bullets": "<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\">\n    <span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Sr. Data Analyst, Highspring India \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span>\n    <span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Oct 2025 - Present</strong></span>\n  </div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Managed complex <strong>requirements engineering</strong> sessions across 4+ stakeholder groups to define transformation rules for pipelines processing 1M+ monthly records.</li>\n    <li>Executed <strong>process mapping</strong> initiatives for 3+ operational workflows, cutting manual overhead by 40% while preserving 95% delivery quality across 15+ launches.</li>\n    <li>Conducted <strong>data flows &amp; API concepts</strong> audits and gap analysis using basic <strong>SQL basics</strong> to resolve 500+ discrepancies, improving stability by 30%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\">\n    <span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Lead Trainer, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span>\n    <span class=\"job-date\"><strong>April 2022 \u2013 Aug 2025</strong></span>\n  </div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Spearheaded structural workflow optimization through comprehensive <strong>back office operations</strong> analysis, boosting hire quality by 84% via <strong>user stories &amp; acceptance criteria</strong>.</li>\n    <li>Deployed self-serve operational metrics using <strong>stakeholder management</strong> strategies, closing knowledge gaps by 30% and lifting team productivity by 25%.</li>\n    <li>Facilitated <strong>UAT coordination</strong> and <strong>agile delivery</strong> cycles for internal HR tools, ensuring rigorous compliance and <strong>auditability &amp; controls</strong> standards.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\">\n    <span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Founder | Creative Director, Maerke Stratcomm \u2013 New Delhi, India</strong></span>\n    <span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Jan 2010 \u2013 Mar 2022</strong></span>\n  </div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Directed end-to-end client engagements focusing on <strong>finance &amp; accounting</strong> structures, scaling HORECA sector sales by 25% through strategic channel alignment.</li>\n    <li>Streamlined digital campaign architectures by translating ambiguous client requests into precise development tasks, accelerating customer acquisition velocity by 30%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>", "exp2_bullets": "", "exp3_bullets": ""}, "clHtml": "<div class=\"letter-meta\">\n  <div class=\"letter-date\">September 29, 2026</div>\n  <div class=\"recipient-block\">\n    <div>Hiring Team</div><div>Turing</div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"subject-line\"><strong>Subject: Application for the Technical Business Analyst Role</strong></div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"salutation\">Dear Hiring Manager,</p>\n<p>I am writing to apply for the Technical Business Analyst role at Turing. What stood out to me in the job description is the focus on turning messy day-to-day operations into clean requirements and clear reports. Before spending the last five years in data analytics, I ran my own small marketing agency for ten years. That mix taught me how much time teams lose when numbers do not match across different tools. Fixing those gaps between business users and engineering is the part of the job I enjoy most.</p>\n<p>Outside of writing SQL queries and building Tableau dashboards, I spend my free time on my terrace in Gurugram growing mushrooms and automating small daily tasks with n8n. Growing mushrooms in North India is not a fancy hobby. It comes down to watching basic details closely. If moisture or airflow slips even a little, the whole batch fails. I bring that same habit to my work when I check data quality, map workflows, or build reports that leaders rely on.</p>\n<p>I also believe analysis is only useful when it solves a real problem on the ground. At Concentrix, our hiring data showed that new joiners were struggling once they started work. Sending another dashboard to management was not fixing the issue. I looked closely at the hiring steps and worked with leadership to bring our training team directly into the interview stage. That simple change improved hire quality by 84 percent. In my current role at Highspring India, I use the same practical approach across four engineering teams to automate recurring reports and cut manual work by 40 percent.</p>\n<p>My day-to-day work covers SQL, Python, Tableau, and working closely with business and tech teams. If the team at Turing uses an internal tool I have not worked with yet, I learn new systems quickly. Practical challenges early in my career taught me how to stay resourceful, focus on the basics, and get things done without hand-holding. When I take ownership of a task, nobody has to follow up twice.</p>\n<p>I would welcome the chance to bring this steady, practical approach to Turing. Thank you for your time and consideration, and I look forward to speaking with you soon.</p>"}, {"sNo": "5", "sNoNum": 5, "resumeId": "RES-5", "company": "Stripe", "industry": "Payments", "jobId": "N/A", "title": "Payments Analyst", "jd": "As a Technical Operations Analyst on the Payments team, you will own the reliability and accuracy of some of the world's most critical payment flows, a platform processing hundreds of billions of dollars annually. You will sit at the intersection of engineering, finance, and operations: triaging live payment failures, driving reconciliation accuracy, and partnering with financial institutions globally to resolve issues fast.\n\nThis is not a passive monitoring role. You will be expected to independently own investigations end-to-end, identify systemic issues before they escalate, and drive process improvements that scale with Stripe's growth.\n\nResponsibilities\nOwn reconciliation and payments-related investigations, ensuring accurate ledgering of funds and resolving discrepancies with banking partners swiftly and precisely.\nProactively monitor payment performance across users and payment methods; triage degradation alerts, diagnose root causes, and communicate findings clearly to technical and non-technical stakeholders.\nServe as the escalation point for complex support inquiries from Technical Account Managers, Product Support, and internal Stripe teams providing fast, well-reasoned resolutions.\nInterface directly with Stripe's global financial partners (card networks, banks, payment processors) to manage operational incidents and drive resolution.\nValidate the accuracy of Stripe's financial data through rigorous analysis and cross-functional collaboration with finance and infrastructure engineering teams.\nIdentify process inefficiencies and lead automation initiatives to reduce manual workload and improve operational throughput at scale.\nBuild and maintain high-quality SOPs, runbooks, and process documentation to ensure institutional knowledge is captured and transferable.\nWho you are\nWe're looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.\n\nMinimum requirements\n3-7 years of experience in a technical operations, payments operations, or financial technology role.\nAdvanced SQL proficiency - you write complex queries (joins, window functions, aggregations) independently and use them as a primary tool for investigation and root cause analysis.\nDeep understanding of end-to-end payment flows - including authorization, clearing, settlement, reconciliation, and exception handling across multiple payment methods and geographies.\nDemonstrated experience investigating and resolving high-severity operational incidents in a payments or financial systems environment with minimal oversight.\nStrong experience working with large-scale financial datasets - validating accuracy, identifying anomalies, and reconciling discrepancies across systems.\nProven ability to manage complex, cross-functional workflows - coordinating simultaneously with engineering, finance, banking partners, and business teams.\nTrack record of identifying process gaps and driving automation or efficiency improvements that meaningfully reduced manual workload.\nExperience writing and maintaining SOPs, runbooks, and technical documentation to a high standard.\nExcellent written and verbal communication in English - able to translate complex technical issues into clear, concise updates for both technical and non-technical audiences.\nComfortable operating with high autonomy in a fast-paced environment, managing competing priorities and time-sensitive deadlines without close supervision.\nPreferred qualifications\nHands-on experience working directly with card networks, acquiring banks, or payment processors, including managing operational escalations and SLA-driven communications.\nExperience with payment cost optimization\nDeep understanding of end-to-end payment flows - including authorization, clearing, settlement, reconciliation, and exception handling across multiple payment methods and geographies.\nFamiliarity with accounting and financial reconciliation principles\nPrior experience in a high-growth fintech or global payments company operating at significant transaction scale.\nExperience building or improving monitoring and alerting frameworks for payment systems.\nPractical history of developing AI-driven solutions designed to automate and optimize high-volume operational workflows.", "location": "Bengaluru", "portal": "Company site", "jdUrl": "https://stripe.com/careers/search", "status": "Applied", "stageBucket": "Applied", "resumeStatus": "Ready for Review", "clStatus": "Not Created", "combinedDocStatus": "To be reviewed", "appliedOn": "8/25/2026", "followUpDate": "", "createdOn": "8/25/2026 09:00 IST", "lastUpdated": "2026-10-06 09:00 IST", "reference": "", "hrName": "", "hrEmail": "", "hrPhone": "", "reviewerNotes": "", "clNotes": "", "generalNotes": "", "aboutCompany": "Global financial infrastructure platform for businesses.", "resumeDriveId": "1SD9swM8eobugH7LB-cYh6cEdBHWNWviU", "resumeLink": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "resumePreviewUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clDriveId": "", "clLink": "", "clPreviewUrl": "", "roleCategory": "payments_operations_analyst", "extractedKeywords": "[object Object]", "revisionCount": 1, "clRevisionCount": 1, "resumeSections": {"summary_html": "<p>Payments Analyst combining a B.Comm in Finance with large-scale operations experience at Google and Concentrix to manage complex <strong>financial reconciliation</strong> and payment flows. Expert in utilizing <strong>advanced SQL</strong> for data validation, anomaly detection, and root cause analysis across global transaction ledgers. Committed to driving operational efficiency and cross-functional incident management to ensure the reliability of high-volume <strong>fintech operations</strong> at Stripe scale.</p>", "skills_html": "<ul>\n  <li><strong>Data Analysis & Database Management:</strong> PostgreSQL, MySQL, BigQuery, Python (Pandas, NumPy), Excel</li>\n  <li><strong>Process Optimization & Data Governance:</strong> Automating wor