20</strong></span>\n  </div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Facilitated detailed <strong>contract review</strong> and vendor negotiations to protect profit margins and accelerate enterprise revenue growth across 50+ client accounts.</li>\n    <li>Optimized end-to-end operational workflows and resource allocation, successfully scaling agency output by 35% through enhanced <strong>operating rigor</strong>.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>", "certifications_html": "<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Tableau Business Intelligence Analyst Professional Certificate</span><span class=\"cert-date\">May 2025</span></div>\n<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Google Advanced Data Analytics</span><span class=\"cert-date\">In Progress</span></div>\n<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Google Project Management</span><span class=\"cert-date\">In Progress</span></div>", "education_html": "<div class=\"edu-row\"><span>University of Delhi, B.Comm(Hons.)</span><span class=\"edu-date\">2013 \u2013 2016</span></div>", "hobbies_html": "<div class=\"hobbies-line\">Practicing Buddhism &nbsp;|&nbsp; Automating life with n8n &nbsp;|&nbsp; Growing Mushrooms</div>"}, "clSections": {"hasStoredCl": true, "salutation_html": "<p class=\"salutation\"><strong>To the Hiring Team at Stripe,</strong></p>", "para1_hook_html": "<p>What caught my attention about the <strong>Financial Analyst, Business F&S</strong> role at Stripe is how directly the job description targets the messy reality of scaling financial operations: establishing clean, consistent reporting foundations and bringing rigorous standardization to opex, headcount, and month-end workflows. Having spent the last several years translating complex operational data into reliable financial insights\u2014preceded by a decade running my own commercial agency\u2014I know that most strategic friction happens when data hygiene breaks down between disparate systems. That operational intersection is precisely where I do my best work.</p>", "para2_stewardship_html": "<p>When I am not profiling millions of records or building reporting dashboards, I spend my spare time on my terrace in Gurugram growing mushrooms and automating personal workflows with <strong>n8n</strong>. Cultivating mushrooms in North India's climate isn't a romantic hobby; it is an exercise in strict variable control\u2014if humidity, airflow, or substrate prep drifts even slightly, the batch fails. I bring that same rigorous stewardship to financial systems, whether I am building <strong>standardized dashboards and data packs</strong> for leadership, running opex budget-versus-actual analysis, or driving <strong>cross-system data integrity</strong> across planning tools.</p>", "para3_impact_story_html": "<p>Furthermore, I believe analysis is only as useful as the operational fix it drives. During my time at Concentrix, our workforce data kept flagging quality drops in new cohorts, and simply sending leadership another dashboard wasn't fixing it. I dug into the operational funnel, traced the disconnect between initial screening and floor realities, and made the case to embed our training team directly into the recruitment workflow. That structural adjustment drove an <strong>84% improvement in hire quality</strong>\u2014similar to how I now partner across <strong>4+ engineering and business groups</strong> at Highspring India to cut manual reporting overhead by 40% and resolve hundreds of data consistency issues.</p>", "para4_resilience_html": "<p>While my background covers strong ground across SQL, Python, Tableau, and financial data modeling, I may not have hands-on experience with every proprietary enterprise tool in your stack on day one. Early in my career, navigating real-world constraints taught me how to be resourceful, focus on fundamentals, and become a <strong>dedicated learner with a sharp focus</strong> on what actually moves the needle. Above all, I am <strong>unconditionally dependable</strong>\u2014when I take ownership of a financial deliverable, you will never have to chase me to see it through.</p>", "para5_closing_html": "<p>I would value the chance to bring this grounded ownership, systems thinking, and steady execution to your F&S team.</p><p>Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to discussing how my experience can support Stripe's upcoming financial and operational initiatives.</p>"}, "index": 7, "role": "Financial Analyst, Business F&S", "category": "monetization_operations_analyst", "jobUrl": "https://stripe.com/careers/search", "jdSnippet": "We are hiring a Financial Analyst for Group Business F&S to build, standardize, and scale the reporting, planning, and process excellence functions that support Group Business Finance & Strategy. This role covers the full spectrum of Group Business F&S financial operations including headcount reporting and analytics, month end close accruals, opex reporting and BvA, business review preparation, and forward-looking planning cycles.\n\nThe immediate and primary mandate is to establish a clean, consistent, and automated reporting foundation across Group Business F&S, bringing discipline and rigor to how financial and workforce data is tracked, packaged, and presented to F&S leadership.\n\nThis is a strong FP&A and Corporate Finance profile. You thrive in building structured processes from the ground up, have a sharp eye for data quality, and bring a standardization and automation-first mindset to everything you touch. You are comfortable working independently, managing a large volume of recurring deliverables with accuracy and timeliness, and continuously improving the processes behind them.\n\nAs you establish the reporting foundation, you will have the opportunity to take on broader scope including owning forecast line items, driving planning cycle inputs, and contributing to more strategic finance work within Group Business F&S.\n\nWhat You'll Do\nReporting and Analytics:\nOwn end-to-end delivery of the monthly and quarterly reporting packages for Group Business F&S, including headcount actuals, opex BvA (budget vs. actual), forecast variance commentary, and trend analysis for MBRs, RTBRs, and board-level reviews\nDesign, build, and maintain standardized dashboards and data packs that give F&S leadership a clear, consistent, and audit-ready view of Group Business F&S financial and workforce health across planning orgs, cost centers, functions, and geographies\nOwn headcount reporting and analytics as a core component of the Group Business F&S reporting suite, tracking HC actuals, variances, and trends alongside broader financial metrics\nEstablish a single source of truth for Group Business F&S data by driving cross-system integrity across Workday, planning systems, and Oracle, defining data quality standards and owning resolution of discrepancies\nTranslate financial and workforce data into clear, concise narratives that explain variances, surface risks, and connect business trends to financial outcomes for senior leaders\nAutomate and streamline recurring reporting workflows, eliminating manual steps and building for scale and consistency\nPlanning and Forecasting: Strategic Ownership\nSupport the annual budget and quarterly forecast processes for Group Business F&S, maintaining and updating financial and HC models by planning org and cost center in Anaplan or any other enterprise planning system\nOver time, take ownership of specific forecast line items within Group Business F&S, building bottoms-up models that incorporate headcount, opex, requisitions, backfill decisions, attrition assumptions, and hire-ahead activity\nBuild scenario models to support F&S leadership in assessing the financial and operational impact of business and workforce decisions across Group Business F&S\nProcess Excellence and Standardization\nLead the documentation and standardization of reporting and planning processes across Group Business F&S, building SOPs, data dictionaries, and process playbooks that ensure consistency, continuity, and auditability\nIdentify inefficiencies across reporting and planning workflows and drive automation initiatives that reduce cycle time and improve output quality\nChampion process improvement opportunities within F&S Bengaluru, bringing proposals to F&S leadership for prioritization and resourcing\nMentor and guide junior analysts in F&S Bengaluru on reporting standards, analytical rigor, and process discipline\nWho You Are\nWe're looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements listed below. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.\n\nMinimum Requirements\n7\u201314 years of progressive experience in FP&A, Corporate Finance, or financial analysis, with meaningful hands-on experience in financial reporting, planning, and process standardization\nBachelor's degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics, Business, or a related field\nStrong FP&A fundamentals: you have owned reporting cycles, built and maintained financial models, and managed budget and forecast processes with precision and without supervision\nProven track record of building and standardizing reporting processes, with a demonstrated ability to bring structure, consistency, and automation to previously manual or fragmented workflows\nExperience in headcount reporting and workforce analytics as part of a broader FP&A or Corporate Finance remit\nCommand of enterprise planning systems such as Anaplan or any equivalent tool for financial and headcount planning; working knowledge of Workday for position and people data is an advantage\nAdvanced Excel and Google Sheets skills, including integrated model design, scenario modeling, and large-dataset manipulation\nDemonstrated ability to translate complex financial and workforce data into clear, concise narratives for senior leaders\nStrong process orientation with a history of building scalable, structured processes in ambiguous or resource-constrained environments\nHigh attention to detail with the discipline to maintain accuracy across high-volume, recurring deliverables under tight deadlines\nExcellent written and verbal communication skills with the ability to work effectively across time zones and with US-based counterparts\nPreferred Qualifications\nExperience in a Finance & Strategy, FP&A, or Corporate Finance function at a high-growth technology or fintech company\nHands-on experience building planning models in Anaplan or any other enterprise planning system (model design and configuration, not just data entry)\nProficiency in SQL or data visualization tools (Tableau, Looker, Hubble, or similar) for building self-service reporting and analytics\nFamiliarity with payroll-to-finance reconciliation, headcount-to-opex bridging, and how HC flows into the P&L\nExperience leading process standardization or automation initiatives within an FP&A or centralized finance team\nExposure to company-wide planning processes including annual planning cycles, board reporting, and forecast submissions\nMBA or professional certifications (CA, CMA, CFA, CPA, CPIM etc.)", "lastUpdate": "2026-10-06 09:00 IST", "referralName": "", "referralContact": "", "referralStatus": "", "resumeFileId": "1ynYWxB0PXGyOI6cFVSUguUQVFFjIbMIS", "resumeUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clFileId": "1_Xnf3sAQ1EY__ROnzeQuF3_LyFGQqQbJ", "clUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "sections": {"summary": "<p>Monetization Operations Analyst combining client-facing expertise with deep analytical rigor to scale revenue streams in the <strong>payments industry</strong>. Proven ability to streamline custom contract onboarding and accelerate collections management through advanced <strong>data analysis</strong> and <strong>process improvement</strong>. Drives operational scaling by fostering cross-functional collaboration and implementing robust <strong>billing systems</strong>.</p>", "skills_html": "<ul>\n  <li><strong>Data Analysis & Database Management:</strong> PostgreSQL, MySQL, Excel, Python (Pandas, NumPy), BigQuery, R, Jupyter Notebooks</li>\n  <li><strong>Process Optimization & Governance:</strong> Automating Workflows, Identifying Improvement Opportunities, Data Cleaning, Wrangling, Transformation, Quality Assurance</li>\n  <li><strong>Business Intelligence & Reporting:</strong> Tableau, Power BI, Dashboard/Report Automation, Interactive Dashboards, Narrative Insight Synthesis, Executive Presentations</li>\n  <li><strong>Stakeholder Collaboration & Soft Skills:</strong> Client Engagement, Cross-Functional Teamwork, Communication, Consulting, Training, Critical Thinking, Problem Solving, Business Acumen</li>\n</ul>", "exp1_bullets": "<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\">\n    <span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Sr. Data Analyst, Highspring India \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span>\n    <span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Oct 2025 - Present</strong></span>\n  </div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Managed complex <strong>billing systems</strong> onboarding and pipelines processing 1M+ monthly records by aligning 4+ stakeholder groups on business transformation rules.</li>\n    <li>Spearheaded <strong>process improvement</strong> initiatives across 3+ operational projects, cutting manual overhead by 40% while maintaining 95% delivery quality over 15+ launches.</li>\n    <li>Conducted rigorous <strong>data analysis</strong> and gap audits using <strong>SQL</strong> queries to resolve 500+ discrepancies, improving operational stability by 30%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\">\n    <span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Lead Trainer, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span>\n    <span class=\"job-date\"><strong>April 2022 \u2013 Aug 2025</strong></span>\n  </div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Executed statistical <strong>collections management</strong> and workflow analyses, spearheading a structural transition that boosted hire quality by 84%.</li>\n    <li>Deployed self-serve operational dashboards to streamline <strong>cross-functional collaboration</strong>, reducing stakeholder knowledge gaps by 30% and increasing productivity by 25%.</li>\n    <li>Delivered <strong>client-facing</strong> presentations and training modules that enforced strict adherence to operating rigor and compliance guidelines for 200+ team members.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\">\n    <span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Founder | Creative Director, Maerke Stratcomm \u2013 New Delhi, India</strong></span>\n    <span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Jan 2010 \u2013 Mar 2020</strong></span>\n  </div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Facilitated detailed <strong>contract review</strong> and vendor negotiations to protect profit margins and accelerate enterprise revenue growth across 50+ client accounts.</li>\n    <li>Optimized end-to-end operational workflows and resource allocation, successfully scaling agency output by 35% through enhanced <strong>operating rigor</strong>.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>", "exp2_bullets": "", "exp3_bullets": ""}, "clHtml": "<p class=\"salutation\"><strong>To the Hiring Team at Stripe,</strong></p>\n<p>What caught my attention about the <strong>Financial Analyst, Business F&S</strong> role at Stripe is how directly the job description targets the messy reality of scaling financial operations: establishing clean, consistent reporting foundations and bringing rigorous standardization to opex, headcount, and month-end workflows. Having spent the last several years translating complex operational data into reliable financial insights\u2014preceded by a decade running my own commercial agency\u2014I know that most strategic friction happens when data hygiene breaks down between disparate systems. That operational intersection is precisely where I do my best work.</p>\n<p>When I am not profiling millions of records or building reporting dashboards, I spend my spare time on my terrace in Gurugram growing mushrooms and automating personal workflows with <strong>n8n</strong>. Cultivating mushrooms in North India's climate isn't a romantic hobby; it is an exercise in strict variable control\u2014if humidity, airflow, or substrate prep drifts even slightly, the batch fails. I bring that same rigorous stewardship to financial systems, whether I am building <strong>standardized dashboards and data packs</strong> for leadership, running opex budget-versus-actual analysis, or driving <strong>cross-system data integrity</strong> across planning tools.</p>\n<p>Furthermore, I believe analysis is only as useful as the operational fix it drives. During my time at Concentrix, our workforce data kept flagging quality drops in new cohorts, and simply sending leadership another dashboard wasn't fixing it. I dug into the operational funnel, traced the disconnect between initial screening and floor realities, and made the case to embed our training team directly into the recruitment workflow. That structural adjustment drove an <strong>84% improvement in hire quality</strong>\u2014similar to how I now partner across <strong>4+ engineering and business groups</strong> at Highspring India to cut manual reporting overhead by 40% and resolve hundreds of data consistency issues.</p>\n<p>While my background covers strong ground across SQL, Python, Tableau, and financial data modeling, I may not have hands-on experience with every proprietary enterprise tool in your stack on day one. Early in my career, navigating real-world constraints taught me how to be resourceful, focus on fundamentals, and become a <strong>dedicated learner with a sharp focus</strong> on what actually moves the needle. Above all, I am <strong>unconditionally dependable</strong>\u2014when I take ownership of a financial deliverable, you will never have to chase me to see it through.</p>\n<p>I would value the chance to bring this grounded ownership, systems thinking, and steady execution to your F&S team.</p><p>Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to discussing how my experience can support Stripe's upcoming financial and operational initiatives.</p>"}, {"sNo": "8", "sNoNum": 8, "resumeId": "RES-8", "company": "United", "industry": "Airlines", "jobId": "GGN00002639", "title": "Analyst - Data Scientist", "jd": "Description\nUnited's Digital Technology team is comprised of many talented individuals all working together with cutting-edge technology to build the best airline in the history of aviation. Our team designs, develops and maintains massively scaling technology solutions brought to life with innovative architectures, data analytics, and digital solutions.\n\n \n\nJob Overview and Responsibilities\n\nThe Data Scientist designs, develops, and implements scalable AI and Generative AI solutions that improve customer experience, business efficiency, and decision-making. The role builds production-grade applications and workflows using Python, SQL, large language models, Retrieval-Augmented Generation, and agentic AI frameworks. It applies advanced analysis, prompt engineering, evaluation, and observability practices to deliver reliable and useful AI capabilities. The role partners with cross-functional teams to translate ambiguous business needs into practical solutions and clearly communicate findings and recommendations.       \n\n \n\n\u2022    Design, develop, test, and deploy robust AI and Generative AI solutions that improve customer experience, operational efficiency, and business decision-making. \n\u2022    Build and deploy production-grade workflows, applications, and data pipelines using Python, SQL, relational databases, and modern AI tools. \n\u2022    Perform advanced exploratory analysis and feature engineering across structured and unstructured datasets to support scalable AI and Generative AI use cases. \n\u2022    Implement prompt engineering strategies, conduct LLM experiments, and apply output evaluation frameworks to ensure quality, relevance, accuracy, safety, and business usefulness.\n\u2022    Develop and scale Retrieval-Augmented Generation pipelines and integrate agentic AI frameworks for multi-step reasoning and workflow automation. \n\u2022    Implement AI observability and MLOps practices to monitor model behavior and system reliability; collaborate with cross-functional teams and communicate findings, risks, and recommendations to stakeholders. \n \n\n \n\n\nThis position is offered on local terms and conditions.  Expatriate assignments and sponsorship for employment visas, even on a time-limited visa status, will not be awarded. This position is for United Airlines Business Services Pvt. Ltd - a wholly owned subsidiary of United Airlines Inc.\n \n\nQualifications\nWhat\u2019s needed to succeed (Minimum Qualifications):\n\u2022    Candidates must hold a Master of Science or equivalent postgraduate degree in a STEM field.\n\u2022    Data Science, Statistics, Engineering, Computer Science, Operations Research, or a related STEM field. \n\u2022    1\u20132 years of industry experience in AI engineering, data science, analytics, or machine learning, including practical experience moving models or analytical workflows toward production. \n\u2022    Strong Python and SQL proficiency; software engineering fundamentals, including Git; experience with large relational datasets and platforms such as Microsoft SQL Server, Snowflake, BigQuery, or Teradata; practical knowledge of LLMs, prompt engineering, embeddings, RAG, and agentic AI; AI observability and MLOps; strong analytical problem-solving; ability to create clear Excel and PowerPoint presentations\n\u2022    Exhibit strong spoken and written communication fluency\n\u2022    Must be legally authorized to work in India for any employer without sponsorship\n \n\n \nWhat will help you propel from the pack (Preferred Qualifications):\n\u2022    Advanced coursework or specialization in machine learning, artificial intelligence, applied statistics, or cloud computing. \n\u2022    Experience deploying Generative AI applications in a production or staging environment, particularly RAG or LLM-based workflows.\n\u2022    Relevant cloud, machine learning, or MLOps certification\n\u2022    Experience with RAGAS or TruLens; LangSmith or MLflow; regression, classification, ensemble methods, and common evaluation metrics; cloud platforms and cloud-based data environments such as AWS, Azure, or GCP.", "location": "Gurugram, Haryana, India", "portal": "Company site", "jdUrl": "https://careers.united.com/us/en/c/corporate-jobs", "status": "Applied", "stageBucket": "Applied", "resumeStatus": "Ready for Review", "clStatus": "Ready for Review", "combinedDocStatus": "To be reviewed", "appliedOn": "8/25/2026", "followUpDate": "", "createdOn": "8/25/2026 09:00 IST", "lastUpdated": "2026-10-07 15:15 IST", "reference": "", "hrName": "", "hrEmail": "", "hrPhone": "", "reviewerNotes": "", "clNotes": "", "generalNotes": "", "aboutCompany": "Major global airline operating Digital Technology & Analytics center in Gurugram.", "resumeDriveId": "1b8O9Z4fjzyQ1V9huamQzT3FROQgdI-P0", "resumeLink": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "resumePreviewUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clDriveId": "134_-e_1KRFXZGy8vzMJsvBw2VMDOadLU", "clLink": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clPreviewUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "roleCategory": "operations_strategy", "extractedKeywords": "[object Object]", "revisionCount": 1, "clRevisionCount": 1, "resumeSections": {"summary_html": "<p>Senior Data &amp; Business Analyst combining extensive enterprise data analytics and operations intelligence experience with a strong foundation in commercial strategy and stakeholder consulting. Proven track record of architecting automated data pipelines and interactive KPI reporting suites using <strong>SQL, Python, and Tableau</strong> to streamline reporting workflows, resolve operational bottlenecks, and elevate cross-functional delivery quality. Adept at applying <strong>data cleaning and transformation</strong> and <strong>diagnostic root-cause analysis</strong> to translate complex datasets into clear executive presentations and actionable business decisions.</p>", "skills_html": "<ul>\n  <li><strong>Data Analysis &amp; Database Management:</strong> SQL (Postgresql, Mysql, Bigquery), Python (Pandas, Numpy), Excel, Api/data Integration, Database Management, R, Jupyter Notebooks</li>\n  <li><strong>Business Intelligence &amp; Visualization:</strong> Dashboard/report Automation, Executive Presentations, KPI Scorecard Design, Tableau, Interactive Dashboards, Narrative Insight Synthesis</li>\n  <li><strong>Data Governance &amp; Process Optimization:</strong> Data Cleaning &amp; Wrangling, Data Transformation, Quality Assurance, Automating Workflows (n8n), Root-cause &amp; Variance Analysis, Identifying Improvement Opportunities</li>\n  <li><strong>Stakeholder Collaboration &amp; Strategy:</strong> Stakeholder Communication, Cross-functional Teamwork, Critical Thinking &amp; Problem Solving, Business Acumen, Consulting &amp; Client Engagement, Training &amp; Mentorship</li>\n</ul>", "experience_html": "<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Sr. Data Analyst, Highspring India \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Oct 2025 - Present</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Spearheaded end-to-end <strong>SQL data modelling</strong> and pipeline optimization across 1M+ monthly records using Python and BigQuery, cutting manual reporting overhead by 40%.</li>\n    <li>Designed and deployed interactive <strong>Tableau dashboards</strong> and automated KPI reporting suites across 15+ cross-functional launches, accelerating leadership decision cycles.</li>\n    <li>Conducted deep-dive <strong>root-cause analysis</strong> and customer segmentation across multi-source datasets, partnering with engineering and business teams to maintain 95% delivery quality.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Lead Trainer, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>April 2022 \u2013 Aug 2025</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Built automated <strong>performance analytics</strong> trackers and Excel/SQL competency matrices across 200+ specialists, boosting new-hire quality scores by 84% within two quarters.</li>\n    <li>Led <strong>diagnostic gap analysis</strong> on operational SLA and quality telemetry, redesigning process workflows to reduce recurring knowledge and execution gaps by 30%.</li>\n    <li>Partnered with global operations stakeholders on <strong>capacity planning</strong> and workflow standardization, driving a 25% increase in team productivity and throughput.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Customer Support Representative, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Jan 2021 \u2013 Mar 2022</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Resolved escalated consumer inquiries by utilizing <strong>CRM telemetry</strong> and historical performance metrics, accelerating ticket resolution speed by 35% across high-volume queues.</li>\n    <li>Analyzed user interaction trends to identify recurring <strong>service bottlenecks</strong>, partnering with operations leads to streamline workflows and boost customer satisfaction.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Founder | Creative Director, Maerke Stratcomm \u2013 New Delhi, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>June 2010 \u2013 July 2020</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Directed <strong>commercial analytics</strong>, pricing strategy, and market segmentation for 15+ B2B and retail clients, driving a 30% increase in customer acquisition.</li>\n    <li>Implemented <strong>funnel performance tracking</strong> and ROI attribution models across regional distribution channels, expanding HORECA and enterprise account revenue by 25%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>", "certifications_html": "<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Tableau Business Intelligence Analyst Professional Certificate</span><span class=\"cert-date\">May 2025</span></div>\n<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Google Advanced Data Analytics</span><span class=\"cert-date\">In Progress</span></div>\n<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Google Project Management</span><span class=\"cert-date\">In Progress</span></div>", "education_html": "<div class=\"edu-row\"><span>University of Delhi, B.Comm(Hons.)</span><span class=\"edu-date\">2013 \u2013 2016</span></div>", "hobbies_html": "<div class=\"hobbies-line\">Practicing Buddhism &nbsp;|&nbsp; Automating life with n8n &nbsp;|&nbsp; Growing Mushrooms</div>"}, "clSections": {"hasStoredCl": true, "salutation_html": "<div class=\"letter-meta\">\n  <div class=\"letter-date\">September 29, 2026</div>\n  <div class=\"recipient-block\">\n    <div>Hiring Manager</div>\n    <div>United</div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"subject-line\"><strong>Re: Application for Analyst - Data Scientist</strong></div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"salutation\">Dear Hiring Manager,</p>", "para1_hook_html": "<p>I am writing to apply for the Analyst - Data Scientist role at United. What stood out to me in the job description is the focus on building practical data workflows and turning messy problems into clear solutions. Before spending the last five years in data analytics, I ran my own small business for ten years. That mix taught me how much time teams lose when numbers do not match across different tools. Fixing those gaps between business needs and technical teams is the part of the job I enjoy most.</p>", "para2_stewardship_html": "<p>Outside of writing Python code and building models, I spend my free time on my terrace in Gurugram growing mushrooms and automating small daily tasks with n8n. Growing mushrooms in North India's weather is not a fancy hobby. It comes down to watching basic details closely. If moisture or airflow slips even a little, the whole batch fails. I bring that same habit to my work when I check data quality, test workflows, or build reliable applications that leaders rely on.</p>", "para3_impact_story_html": "<p>I also believe analysis is only useful when it solves a real problem on the ground. At Concentrix, our hiring data showed that new joiners were struggling once they started work. Sending another dashboard to management was not fixing the issue. I looked closely at the hiring steps and worked with leadership to bring our training team directly into the interview stage. That simple change improved hire quality by 84%. In my current role at Highspring India, I use the same practical approach across four engineering teams to automate recurring reports and cut manual work by 40%.</p>", "para4_resilience_html": "<p>My day-to-day work covers SQL, Python, and working closely with business and tech teams. If your team uses an internal tool I have not worked with yet, I learn new systems quickly. Practical challenges early in my career taught me how to stay resourceful and get things done without hand-holding. When I take ownership of a task, you will not have to follow up twice.</p>", "para5_closing_html": "<p>I would welcome the chance to bring this steady, practical approach to your team. Thank you for your time and consideration, and I look forward to speaking with you soon.</p>"}, "index": 8, "role": "Analyst - Data Scientist", "category": "operations_strategy", "jobUrl": "https://careers.united.com/us/en/c/corporate-jobs", "jdSnippet": "Description\nUnited's Digital Technology team is comprised of many talented individuals all working together with cutting-edge technology to build the best airline in the history of aviation. Our team designs, develops and maintains massively scaling technology solutions brought to life with innovative architectures, data analytics, and digital solutions.\n\n \n\nJob Overview and Responsibilities\n\nThe Data Scientist designs, develops, and implements scalable AI and Generative AI solutions that improve customer experience, business efficiency, and decision-making. The role builds production-grade applications and workflows using Python, SQL, large language models, Retrieval-Augmented Generation, and agentic AI frameworks. It applies advanced analysis, prompt engineering, evaluation, and observability practices to deliver reliable and useful AI capabilities. The role partners with cross-functional teams to translate ambiguous business needs into practical solutions and clearly communicate findings and recommendations.       \n\n \n\n\u2022    Design, develop, test, and deploy robust AI and Generative AI solutions that improve customer experience, operational efficiency, and business decision-making. \n\u2022    Build and deploy production-grade workflows, applications, and data pipelines using Python, SQL, relational databases, and modern AI tools. \n\u2022    Perform advanced exploratory analysis and feature engineering across structured and unstructured datasets to support scalable AI and Generative AI use cases. \n\u2022    Implement prompt engineering strategies, conduct LLM experiments, and apply output evaluation frameworks to ensure quality, relevance, accuracy, safety, and business usefulness.\n\u2022    Develop and scale Retrieval-Augmented Generation pipelines and integrate agentic AI frameworks for multi-step reasoning and workflow automation. \n\u2022    Implement AI observability and MLOps practices to monitor model behavior and system reliability; collaborate with cross-functional teams and communicate findings, risks, and recommendations to stakeholders. \n \n\n \n\n\nThis position is offered on local terms and conditions.  Expatriate assignments and sponsorship for employment visas, even on a time-limited visa status, will not be awarded. This position is for United Airlines Business Services Pvt. Ltd - a wholly owned subsidiary of United Airlines Inc.\n \n\nQualifications\nWhat\u2019s needed to succeed (Minimum Qualifications):\n\u2022    Candidates must hold a Master of Science or equivalent postgraduate degree in a STEM field.\n\u2022    Data Science, Statistics, Engineering, Computer Science, Operations Research, or a related STEM field. \n\u2022    1\u20132 years of industry experience in AI engineering, data science, analytics, or machine learning, including practical experience moving models or analytical workflows toward production. \n\u2022    Strong Python and SQL proficiency; software engineering fundamentals, including Git; experience with large relational datasets and platforms such as Microsoft SQL Server, Snowflake, BigQuery, or Teradata; practical knowledge of LLMs, prompt engineering, embeddings, RAG, and agentic AI; AI observability and MLOps; strong analytical problem-solving; ability to create clear Excel and PowerPoint presentations\n\u2022    Exhibit strong spoken and written communication fluency\n\u2022    Must be legally authorized to work in India for any employer without sponsorship\n \n\n \nWhat will help you propel from the pack (Preferred Qualifications):\n\u2022    Advanced coursework or specialization in machine learning, artificial intelligence, applied statistics, or cloud computing. \n\u2022    Experience deploying Generative AI applications in a production or staging environment, particularly RAG or LLM-based workflows.\n\u2022    Relevant cloud, machine learning, or MLOps certification\n\u2022    Experience with RAGAS or TruLens; LangSmith or MLflow; regression, classification, ensemble methods, and common evaluation metrics; cloud platforms and cloud-based data environments such as AWS, Azure, or GCP.", "lastUpdate": "2026-10-07 15:15 IST", "referralName": "", "referralContact": "", "referralStatus": "", "resumeFileId": "1b8O9Z4fjzyQ1V9huamQzT3FROQgdI-P0", "resumeUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clFileId": "134_-e_1KRFXZGy8vzMJsvBw2VMDOadLU", "clUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "sections": {"summary": "<p>Senior Data &amp; Business Analyst combining extensive enterprise data analytics and operations intelligence experience with a strong foundation in commercial strategy and stakeholder consulting. Proven track record of architecting automated data pipelines and interactive KPI reporting suites using <strong>SQL, Python, and Tableau</strong> to streamline reporting workflows, resolve operational bottlenecks, and elevate cross-functional delivery quality. Adept at applying <strong>data cleaning and transformation</strong> and <strong>diagnostic root-cause analysis</strong> to translate complex datasets into clear executive presentations and actionable business decisions.</p>", "skills_html": "<ul>\n  <li><strong>Data Analysis &amp; Database Management:</strong> SQL (Postgresql, Mysql, Bigquery), Python (Pandas, Numpy), Excel, Api/data Integration, Database Management, R, Jupyter Notebooks</li>\n  <li><strong>Business Intelligence &amp; Visualization:</strong> Dashboard/report Automation, Executive Presentations, KPI Scorecard Design, Tableau, Interactive Dashboards, Narrative Insight Synthesis</li>\n  <li><strong>Data Governance &amp; Process Optimization:</strong> Data Cleaning &amp; Wrangling, Data Transformation, Quality Assurance, Automating Workflows (n8n), Root-cause &amp; Variance Analysis, Identifying Improvement Opportunities</li>\n  <li><strong>Stakeholder Collaboration &amp; Strategy:</strong> Stakeholder Communication, Cross-functional Teamwork, Critical Thinking &amp; Problem Solving, Business Acumen, Consulting &amp; Client Engagement, Training &amp; Mentorship</li>\n</ul>", "exp1_bullets": "<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Sr. Data Analyst, Highspring India \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Oct 2025 - Present</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Spearheaded end-to-end <strong>SQL data modelling</strong> and pipeline optimization across 1M+ monthly records using Python and BigQuery, cutting manual reporting overhead by 40%.</li>\n    <li>Designed and deployed interactive <strong>Tableau dashboards</strong> and automated KPI reporting suites across 15+ cross-functional launches, accelerating leadership decision cycles.</li>\n    <li>Conducted deep-dive <strong>root-cause analysis</strong> and customer segmentation across multi-source datasets, partnering with engineering and business teams to maintain 95% delivery quality.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Lead Trainer, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>April 2022 \u2013 Aug 2025</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Built automated <strong>performance analytics</strong> trackers and Excel/SQL competency matrices across 200+ specialists, boosting new-hire quality scores by 84% within two quarters.</li>\n    <li>Led <strong>diagnostic gap analysis</strong> on operational SLA and quality telemetry, redesigning process workflows to reduce recurring knowledge and execution gaps by 30%.</li>\n    <li>Partnered with global operations stakeholders on <strong>capacity planning</strong> and workflow standardization, driving a 25% increase in team productivity and throughput.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Customer Support Representative, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Jan 2021 \u2013 Mar 2022</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Resolved escalated consumer inquiries by utilizing <strong>CRM telemetry</strong> and historical performance metrics, accelerating ticket resolution speed by 35% across high-volume queues.</li>\n    <li>Analyzed user interaction trends to identify recurring <strong>service bottlenecks</strong>, partnering with operations leads to streamline workflows and boost customer satisfaction.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Founder | Creative Director, Maerke Stratcomm \u2013 New Delhi, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>June 2010 \u2013 July 2020</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Directed <strong>commercial analytics</strong>, pricing strategy, and market segmentation for 15+ B2B and retail clients, driving a 30% increase in customer acquisition.</li>\n    <li>Implemented <strong>funnel performance tracking</strong> and ROI attribution models across regional distribution channels, expanding HORECA and enterprise account revenue by 25%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>", "exp2_bullets": "", "exp3_bullets": ""}, "clHtml": "<div class=\"letter-meta\">\n  <div class=\"letter-date\">September 29, 2026</div>\n  <div class=\"recipient-block\">\n    <div>Hiring Manager</div>\n    <div>United</div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"subject-line\"><strong>Re: Application for Analyst - Data Scientist</strong></div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"salutation\">Dear Hiring Manager,</p>\n<p>I am writing to apply for the Analyst - Data Scientist role at United. What stood out to me in the job description is the focus on building practical data workflows and turning messy problems into clear solutions. Before spending the last five years in data analytics, I ran my own small business for ten years. That mix taught me how much time teams lose when numbers do not match across different tools. Fixing those gaps between business needs and technical teams is the part of the job I enjoy most.</p>\n<p>Outside of writing Python code and building models, I spend my free time on my terrace in Gurugram growing mushrooms and automating small daily tasks with n8n. Growing mushrooms in North India's weather is not a fancy hobby. It comes down to watching basic details closely. If moisture or airflow slips even a little, the whole batch fails. I bring that same habit to my work when I check data quality, test workflows, or build reliable applications that leaders rely on.</p>\n<p>I also believe analysis is only useful when it solves a real problem on the ground. At Concentrix, our hiring data showed that new joiners were struggling once they started work. Sending another dashboard to management was not fixing the issue. I looked closely at the hiring steps and worked with leadership to bring our training team directly into the interview stage. That simple change improved hire quality by 84%. In my current role at Highspring India, I use the same practical approach across four engineering teams to automate recurring reports and cut manual work by 40%.</p>\n<p>My day-to-day work covers SQL, Python, and working closely with business and tech teams. If your team uses an internal tool I have not worked with yet, I learn new systems quickly. Practical challenges early in my career taught me how to stay resourceful and get things done without hand-holding. When I take ownership of a task, you will not have to follow up twice.</p>\n<p>I would welcome the chance to bring this steady, practical approach to your team. Thank you for your time and consideration, and I look forward to speaking with you soon.</p>"}, {"sNo": "9", "sNoNum": 9, "resumeId": "RES-9", "company": "United", "industry": "Airlines", "jobId": "Job IdGGN00002622", "title": "Senior Analyst - Finance Data Capability", "jd": "Description\nThis role sits at the intersection of Finance, Data, and AI, enabling the transformation of finance data into a strategic, intelligence-driven asset. It supports the design, governance, and activation of finance data capabilities to deliver faster insights, improved decision-making, and scalable business value.\n\nThe role will drive adoption of modern data platforms, while actively exploring and embedding GenAI and agentic solutions to automate workflows, enhance analytics, and enable intelligent, self-service finance operations. Working closely with Finance and Digital Technology teams, this position contributes to building an AI-enabled finance ecosystem that is standardized, efficient, and future-ready.\n\nJob Overview and Responsibilities\n\n1. Support Enterprise-Wide Data Standards, Analytics, and Insights\n\nSupport cross-functional collaborations to assess and redesign finance data processes and technical landscapes, focusing on simplification, standardization, and end-to-end optimization aligned with enterprise goals\nWork with large and complex (big) data sets across finance domains, ensuring scalable handling, efficient processing, and performance optimization across systems and data platforms\nEvaluate and embed GenAI and agentic solutions (e.g., copilots, autonomous workflows, intelligent pipelines) to reimagine finance processes, reduce manual effort, and accelerate decision-making cycles\nDrive adoption of modern data and automation tools (Data Platforms, Oracle, Alteryx, Tableau), augmenting them with AI-driven insights, predictive analytics, and intelligent automation\nDevelop and maintain financial data products, standardized KPIs, reusable datasets, and robust, dynamic data structures (e.g., scalable data models, semantic layers) to support evolving business needs and AI consumption\nMaintain and validate finance data mappings, transformation logic, and integrations, while exploring AI-assisted reconciliation, mapping automation, and anomaly detection\nSupport finance data governance by defining data quality rules and partnering on controls and lineage, leveraging AI for continuous monitoring, exception handling, and automated remediation insights\n2. Support financial transformation initiatives\n\nCollaborate cross-functionally to support finance data transformation initiatives, incorporating AI-first design principles, scalable data structures, and automation opportunities into solution architecture\n\nPartner with stakeholders (DT, Finance, etc.) to ensure alignment with enterprise strategy, including identification and prioritization of GenAI, agentic workflows, and big data use cases\n\nSupport delivery of transformation initiatives (milestones, timelines, reporting), while piloting and scaling agent-based workflows and AI-enabled process automation\n\nContribute to business cases by quantifying impact from AI, automation, and improved data architecture (e.g., scalability, speed, accuracy, and cost efficiency\n \n\nThis position is offered on local terms and conditions.  Expatriate assignments and sponsorship for employment visas, even on a time-limited visa status, will not be awarded. This position is for United Airlines Business Services Pvt. Ltd - a wholly owned subsidiary of United Airlines Inc.\n\nQualifications\nWhat\u2019s needed to succeed (Minimum Qualifications):\n\nBachelor's degree\nFinance, Accounting, Information Systems, Computer Science, or related field\n4+ years of finance and/or technology experience\nExperience in Finance Analytics, Data Analytics, Finance Systems, or Technology Transformation\nStrong expertise in finance data, reporting, analytics, data modeling, and master data governance\nExperience working with large, complex datasets using platforms such as Databricks, Snowflake, Foundry, SQL Server\nHands-on experience with Tableau and/or Tableau for reporting and visualization\nMust have working knowledge of Oracle EDM, complimentary would be Oracle ERP, Oracle EPM\nStrong proficiency in SQL and data analysis\nExperience using Python for analytics, automation, or process improvement\nExperience with Alteryx or similar ETL/data transformation tools\nFamiliarity with GenAI tools (e.g., Copilot, ChatGPT), AI-assisted analytics, and agentic workflows/intelligent automation\nStrong analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills, with the ability to translate complex data into actionable business insights\nAbility to independently identify and implement opportunities to improve finance processes through data, automation, AI, and scalable technology solutions, AI, and scalable technology solutions\nExcellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to present complex data, AI-driven insights, and process improvements to both finance and non-finance stakeholders\nStrong understanding of how people, processes, data, and technology (including AI/automation) come together to build scalable and sustainable capabilities\nAbility to work independently and proactively identify opportunities to embed AI, automation, and improved data structures into existing workflows\n \nWhat will help you propel from the pack (Preferred Qualifications):\n\nMaster's degree\nMasters of Business Administration\nExperience in airline or similar industry\nExperience with PMO/project management tools such as Smartsheet, JIRA, or similar platforms\nUnderstanding of finance data standards, governance, controls, and business processes across domains such as GL, AP, AR, FP&A, and Treasury.\nExperience establishing or driving data definitions, business rules, and reporting standards across functions\nExposure to cloud-based data and analytics architectures (e.g., AWS Data Lake, Azure, or similar platforms).", "location": "Gurugram, Haryana, India", "portal": "Company site", "jdUrl": "https://careers.united.com/us/en/c/corporate-jobs", "status": "Applied", "stageBucket": "Applied", "resumeStatus": "Ready for Review", "clStatus": "Not Created", "combinedDocStatus": "", "appliedOn": "8/25/2026", "followUpDate": "", "createdOn": "8/25/2026 09:00 IST", "lastUpdated": "2026-10-07 15:15 IST", "reference": "", "h