ustomer Support Representative, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Jan 2021 \u2013 Mar 2022</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Resolved escalated consumer inquiries by utilizing <strong>CRM telemetry</strong> and historical performance metrics, accelerating ticket resolution speed by 35% across high-volume queues.</li>\n    <li>Analyzed user interaction trends to identify recurring <strong>service bottlenecks</strong>, partnering with operations leads to streamline workflows and boost customer satisfaction.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Founder | Creative Director, Maerke Stratcomm \u2013 New Delhi, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>June 2010 \u2013 July 2020</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Directed <strong>commercial analytics</strong>, pricing strategy, and market segmentation for 15+ B2B and retail clients, driving a 30% increase in customer acquisition.</li>\n    <li>Implemented <strong>funnel performance tracking</strong> and ROI attribution models across regional distribution channels, expanding HORECA and enterprise account revenue by 25%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>", "certifications_html": "<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Tableau Business Intelligence Analyst Professional Certificate</span><span class=\"cert-date\">May 2025</span></div>\n<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Google Advanced Data Analytics</span><span class=\"cert-date\">In Progress</span></div>\n<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Google Project Management</span><span class=\"cert-date\">In Progress</span></div>", "education_html": "<div class=\"edu-row\"><span>University of Delhi, B.Comm(Hons.)</span><span class=\"edu-date\">2013 \u2013 2016</span></div>", "hobbies_html": "<div class=\"hobbies-line\">Practicing Buddhism &nbsp;|&nbsp; Automating life with n8n &nbsp;|&nbsp; Growing Mushrooms</div>"}, "clSections": {"hasStoredCl": false, "salutation_html": "<p class=\"salutation\">Dear Hiring Manager at United,</p>", "para1_hook_html": "<p>I am writing to apply for the Senior Analyst - Finance Data Capability role at United. With over five years of hands-on experience building reliable SQL and Python reporting pipelines, designing executive Tableau dashboards, and partnering with product and operations leaders, I am eager to contribute immediately to United's data and analytics goals.</p>", "para2_stewardship_html": "<p>Throughout my career across high-volume operational and business intelligence environments, I have focused on turning complex, fragmented datasets into clear, trustworthy decision frameworks. Whether automating recurring ETL workflows or establishing governed KPI definitions across teams, I prioritize data accuracy and practical business impact.</p>", "para3_impact_story_html": "<p>In my recent work, I re-engineered manual reporting workflows into automated SQL and Tableau pipelines that reduced reporting latency by over 40% while uncovering key drivers of funnel conversion and SLA performance. This blend of technical execution and stakeholder communication aligns closely with what United seeks in this position.</p>", "para4_resilience_html": "<p>I thrive in fast-paced environments where requirements evolve quickly and cross-functional clarity is essential. My background spans end-to-end requirement gathering, UAT governance, root-cause diagnostics, and translating technical findings for non-technical leadership.</p>", "para5_closing_html": "<p>Thank you for your time and consideration. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my background in SQL, Python, Tableau, and business analysis can support United's upcoming initiatives.</p>"}, "index": 9, "role": "Senior Analyst - Finance Data Capability", "category": "data_engineering_modelling", "jobUrl": "https://careers.united.com/us/en/c/corporate-jobs", "jdSnippet": "Description\nThis role sits at the intersection of Finance, Data, and AI, enabling the transformation of finance data into a strategic, intelligence-driven asset. It supports the design, governance, and activation of finance data capabilities to deliver faster insights, improved decision-making, and scalable business value.\n\nThe role will drive adoption of modern data platforms, while actively exploring and embedding GenAI and agentic solutions to automate workflows, enhance analytics, and enable intelligent, self-service finance operations. Working closely with Finance and Digital Technology teams, this position contributes to building an AI-enabled finance ecosystem that is standardized, efficient, and future-ready.\n\nJob Overview and Responsibilities\n\n1. Support Enterprise-Wide Data Standards, Analytics, and Insights\n\nSupport cross-functional collaborations to assess and redesign finance data processes and technical landscapes, focusing on simplification, standardization, and end-to-end optimization aligned with enterprise goals\nWork with large and complex (big) data sets across finance domains, ensuring scalable handling, efficient processing, and performance optimization across systems and data platforms\nEvaluate and embed GenAI and agentic solutions (e.g., copilots, autonomous workflows, intelligent pipelines) to reimagine finance processes, reduce manual effort, and accelerate decision-making cycles\nDrive adoption of modern data and automation tools (Data Platforms, Oracle, Alteryx, Tableau), augmenting them with AI-driven insights, predictive analytics, and intelligent automation\nDevelop and maintain financial data products, standardized KPIs, reusable datasets, and robust, dynamic data structures (e.g., scalable data models, semantic layers) to support evolving business needs and AI consumption\nMaintain and validate finance data mappings, transformation logic, and integrations, while exploring AI-assisted reconciliation, mapping automation, and anomaly detection\nSupport finance data governance by defining data quality rules and partnering on controls and lineage, leveraging AI for continuous monitoring, exception handling, and automated remediation insights\n2. Support financial transformation initiatives\n\nCollaborate cross-functionally to support finance data transformation initiatives, incorporating AI-first design principles, scalable data structures, and automation opportunities into solution architecture\n\nPartner with stakeholders (DT, Finance, etc.) to ensure alignment with enterprise strategy, including identification and prioritization of GenAI, agentic workflows, and big data use cases\n\nSupport delivery of transformation initiatives (milestones, timelines, reporting), while piloting and scaling agent-based workflows and AI-enabled process automation\n\nContribute to business cases by quantifying impact from AI, automation, and improved data architecture (e.g., scalability, speed, accuracy, and cost efficiency\n \n\nThis position is offered on local terms and conditions.  Expatriate assignments and sponsorship for employment visas, even on a time-limited visa status, will not be awarded. This position is for United Airlines Business Services Pvt. Ltd - a wholly owned subsidiary of United Airlines Inc.\n\nQualifications\nWhat\u2019s needed to succeed (Minimum Qualifications):\n\nBachelor's degree\nFinance, Accounting, Information Systems, Computer Science, or related field\n4+ years of finance and/or technology experience\nExperience in Finance Analytics, Data Analytics, Finance Systems, or Technology Transformation\nStrong expertise in finance data, reporting, analytics, data modeling, and master data governance\nExperience working with large, complex datasets using platforms such as Databricks, Snowflake, Foundry, SQL Server\nHands-on experience with Tableau and/or Tableau for reporting and visualization\nMust have working knowledge of Oracle EDM, complimentary would be Oracle ERP, Oracle EPM\nStrong proficiency in SQL and data analysis\nExperience using Python for analytics, automation, or process improvement\nExperience with Alteryx or similar ETL/data transformation tools\nFamiliarity with GenAI tools (e.g., Copilot, ChatGPT), AI-assisted analytics, and agentic workflows/intelligent automation\nStrong analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills, with the ability to translate complex data into actionable business insights\nAbility to independently identify and implement opportunities to improve finance processes through data, automation, AI, and scalable technology solutions, AI, and scalable technology solutions\nExcellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to present complex data, AI-driven insights, and process improvements to both finance and non-finance stakeholders\nStrong understanding of how people, processes, data, and technology (including AI/automation) come together to build scalable and sustainable capabilities\nAbility to work independently and proactively identify opportunities to embed AI, automation, and improved data structures into existing workflows\n \nWhat will help you propel from the pack (Preferred Qualifications):\n\nMaster's degree\nMasters of Business Administration\nExperience in airline or similar industry\nExperience with PMO/project management tools such as Smartsheet, JIRA, or similar platforms\nUnderstanding of finance data standards, governance, controls, and business processes across domains such as GL, AP, AR, FP&A, and Treasury.\nExperience establishing or driving data definitions, business rules, and reporting standards across functions\nExposure to cloud-based data and analytics architectures (e.g., AWS Data Lake, Azure, or similar platforms).", "lastUpdate": "2026-10-07 15:15 IST", "referralName": "", "referralContact": "", "referralStatus": "", "resumeFileId": "1t4igDaM2UMlET9PNovs_RzuawiCYhgLY", "resumeUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clFileId": "", "clUrl": "", "sections": {"summary": "<p>Senior Data &amp; Business Analyst combining extensive enterprise data analytics and operations intelligence experience with a strong foundation in commercial strategy and stakeholder consulting. Proven track record of leveraging <strong>SQL, Python, and Tableau</strong> for financial reconciliation, commercial pricing analysis, and automated KPI governance across enterprise and regional operations. Adept at applying <strong>data cleaning and transformation</strong> and <strong>automated dashboard reporting</strong> to translate complex datasets into clear executive presentations and actionable business decisions.</p>", "skills_html": "<ul>\n  <li><strong>Data Analysis &amp; Database Management:</strong> Api/data Integration, SQL (Postgresql, Mysql, Bigquery), Python (Pandas, Numpy), Excel, Database Management, R, Jupyter Notebooks</li>\n  <li><strong>Business Intelligence &amp; Visualization:</strong> Dashboard/report Automation, KPI Scorecard Design, Tableau, Narrative Insight Synthesis, Interactive Dashboards, Executive Presentations</li>\n  <li><strong>Data Governance &amp; Process Optimization:</strong> Data Transformation, Identifying Improvement Opportunities, Data Cleaning &amp; Wrangling, Quality Assurance, Automating Workflows (n8n), Root-cause &amp; Variance Analysis</li>\n  <li><strong>Stakeholder Collaboration &amp; Strategy:</strong> Stakeholder Communication, Cross-functional Teamwork, Critical Thinking &amp; Problem Solving, Business Acumen, Consulting &amp; Client Engagement, Training &amp; Mentorship</li>\n</ul>", "exp1_bullets": "<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Sr. Data Analyst, Highspring India \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Oct 2025 - Present</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Spearheaded end-to-end <strong>data profiling and reconciliation</strong> across 1M+ monthly records using SQL and Python, resolving reporting discrepancies and cutting manual overhead by 40%.</li>\n    <li>Designed and deployed interactive <strong>Tableau dashboards</strong> and automated KPI reporting suites across 15+ cross-functional launches, accelerating leadership decision cycles.</li>\n    <li>Conducted deep-dive <strong>root-cause analysis</strong> and customer segmentation across multi-source datasets, partnering with engineering and business teams to maintain 95% delivery quality.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Lead Trainer, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>April 2022 \u2013 Aug 2025</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Built automated <strong>performance analytics</strong> trackers and Excel/SQL competency matrices across 200+ specialists, boosting new-hire quality scores by 84% within two quarters.</li>\n    <li>Led <strong>diagnostic gap analysis</strong> on operational SLA and quality telemetry, redesigning process workflows to reduce recurring knowledge and execution gaps by 30%.</li>\n    <li>Partnered with global operations stakeholders on <strong>capacity planning</strong> and workflow standardization, driving a 25% increase in team productivity and throughput.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Customer Support Representative, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Jan 2021 \u2013 Mar 2022</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Resolved escalated consumer inquiries by utilizing <strong>CRM telemetry</strong> and historical performance metrics, accelerating ticket resolution speed by 35% across high-volume queues.</li>\n    <li>Analyzed user interaction trends to identify recurring <strong>service bottlenecks</strong>, partnering with operations leads to streamline workflows and boost customer satisfaction.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Founder | Creative Director, Maerke Stratcomm \u2013 New Delhi, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>June 2010 \u2013 July 2020</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Directed <strong>commercial analytics</strong>, pricing strategy, and market segmentation for 15+ B2B and retail clients, driving a 30% increase in customer acquisition.</li>\n    <li>Implemented <strong>funnel performance tracking</strong> and ROI attribution models across regional distribution channels, expanding HORECA and enterprise account revenue by 25%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>", "exp2_bullets": "", "exp3_bullets": ""}, "clHtml": "<p class=\"salutation\">Dear Hiring Manager at United,</p>\n<p>I am writing to apply for the Senior Analyst - Finance Data Capability role at United. With over five years of hands-on experience building reliable SQL and Python reporting pipelines, designing executive Tableau dashboards, and partnering with product and operations leaders, I am eager to contribute immediately to United's data and analytics goals.</p>\n<p>Throughout my career across high-volume operational and business intelligence environments, I have focused on turning complex, fragmented datasets into clear, trustworthy decision frameworks. Whether automating recurring ETL workflows or establishing governed KPI definitions across teams, I prioritize data accuracy and practical business impact.</p>\n<p>In my recent work, I re-engineered manual reporting workflows into automated SQL and Tableau pipelines that reduced reporting latency by over 40% while uncovering key drivers of funnel conversion and SLA performance. This blend of technical execution and stakeholder communication aligns closely with what United seeks in this position.</p>\n<p>I thrive in fast-paced environments where requirements evolve quickly and cross-functional clarity is essential. My background spans end-to-end requirement gathering, UAT governance, root-cause diagnostics, and translating technical findings for non-technical leadership.</p>\n<p>Thank you for your time and consideration. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my background in SQL, Python, Tableau, and business analysis can support United's upcoming initiatives.</p>"}, {"sNo": "10", "sNoNum": 10, "resumeId": "RES-10", "company": "United", "industry": "Airlines", "jobId": "Job IdGGN00002647", "title": "Analyst - Catering Systems Administrator", "jd": "Description\nJob Overview and Responsibilities\n\nThe Analyst - Catering Systems Administrator plays a critical role in maintaining the integrity and accuracy of catering data across United\u2019s systems and tools. This position supports business partners in delivering seamless catering services for flights systemwide through meticulous data management, system administration, and process optimization.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n\u2022 Data Management & Quality Assurance: Enter, verify, and maintain accurate catering data in United\u2019s management systems, ensuring timely updates with the precision required to support operational excellence\n\n\u2022 System Architecture & Configuration: Design and build system framework and codes to optimize service scheduling and ensure accurate vendor payments across the catering network\n\n\u2022 Data Integrity & Error Resolution: Conduct comprehensive data audits, identify inconsistencies, and collaborate with stakeholders to resolve issues while maintaining the highest standards of data quality\n\n\u2022 Technical Issue Resolution: Serve as a liaison between internal and external stakeholders to report, monitor, and resolve technical challenges efficiently\n\n\u2022 Process Improvement: Develop and implement scalable process enhancements that drive operational efficiency and organizational agility\n\n\u2022 Systems Administration: Oversee system setup, maintenance, vendor access management, and corporate compliance requirements\n\n\u2022 Cross-Functional Collaboration: Partner with diverse teams and external vendors to support ad-hoc projects and ensure operational accuracy\n\n \n\nThis position is offered on local terms and conditions.  Expatriate assignments and sponsorship for employment visas, even on a time-limited visa status, will not be awarded. This position is for United Airlines Business Services Pvt. Ltd - a wholly owned subsidiary of United Airlines Inc.\n\n \n\nQualifications\nQualifications\n\nRequired Qualifications:\n\n\u2022 Bachelor\u2019s degree in Hospitality, Business Administration, or related field\n\n\u2022 3+ years of experience in data entry and administrative support for large-scale teams and systems\n\n\u2022 Exceptional attention to detail and accuracy\n\n\u2022 Strong analytical and data management capabilities\n\n\u2022 Proven ability to work effectively across multiple stakeholder groups\n\n\u2022 Self-motivated with the ability to work independently in a remote environment\n\n\u2022 Excellent written and verbal communication skills\n\n\u2022 Solution-oriented mindset with strong problem-solving abilities\n\n\u2022 Legal authorization to work in India without sponsorship requirements\n\n\u2022 Fluency in English (written and spoken)\n\n\u2022 Ability to lead projects\n\nPreferred Qualifications:\n\n\u2022 Advanced degree or specialization in Hospitality, Catering/Food Services, or Airline Industry\n\n\u00b7  Experience using AI tools like Copilot, Gemini etc.\n\n\u2022 Technical proficiency in SQL and Python\n\n\u2022 Knowledge of airport or airline catering operations\n\n\u2022 Experience with continuous improvement methodologies\n\n\u2022 Familiarity with enterprise management systems (Oracle, CAE, Coupa, SAP, etc.)", "location": "Gurugram, Haryana, India", "portal": "Company site", "jdUrl": "https://careers.united.com/us/en/c/corporate-jobs", "status": "Applied", "stageBucket": "Applied", "resumeStatus": "Ready for Review"