designing process workflows to reduce recurring knowledge and execution gaps by 30%.</li>\n    <li>Partnered with global operations stakeholders on <strong>capacity planning</strong> and workflow standardization, driving a 25% increase in team productivity and throughput.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Customer Support Representative, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Jan 2021 \u2013 Mar 2022</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Resolved escalated consumer inquiries by utilizing <strong>CRM telemetry</strong> and historical performance metrics, accelerating ticket resolution speed by 35% across high-volume queues.</li>\n    <li>Analyzed user interaction trends to identify recurring <strong>service bottlenecks</strong>, partnering with operations leads to streamline workflows and boost customer satisfaction.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Founder | Creative Director, Maerke Stratcomm \u2013 New Delhi, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>June 2010 \u2013 July 2020</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Directed <strong>commercial analytics</strong>, pricing strategy, and market segmentation for 15+ B2B and retail clients, driving a 30% increase in customer acquisition.</li>\n    <li>Implemented <strong>funnel performance tracking</strong> and ROI attribution models across regional distribution channels, expanding HORECA and enterprise account revenue by 25%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>", "certifications_html": "<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Tableau Business Intelligence Analyst Professional Certificate</span><span class=\"cert-date\">May 2025</span></div>\n<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Google Advanced Data Analytics</span><span class=\"cert-date\">In Progress</span></div>\n<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Google Project Management</span><span class=\"cert-date\">In Progress</span></div>", "education_html": "<div class=\"edu-row\"><span>University of Delhi, B.Comm(Hons.)</span><span class=\"edu-date\">2013 \u2013 2016</span></div>", "hobbies_html": "<div class=\"hobbies-line\">Practicing Buddhism &nbsp;|&nbsp; Automating life with n8n &nbsp;|&nbsp; Growing Mushrooms</div>"}, "clSections": {"hasStoredCl": true, "salutation_html": "<p class=\"salutation\"><strong>To the Hiring Team at United,</strong></p>", "para1_hook_html": "<p>What caught my attention about the <strong>Analyst - Catering Systems Administrator</strong> role at United is how directly it addresses the behind-the-scenes precision required to keep a massive operational network moving. Ensuring accurate data, vendor payments, and seamless system configurations across flight catering requires an analytical eye that respects how small data errors compound at scale. Having spent the last several years turning messy operational workflows into clean data models and structured BI\u2014preceded by a decade running my own commercial operations and B2B sales\u2014I know that logistical reliability lives or dies in the details of the database.</p>", "para2_stewardship_html": "<p>When I am not writing <strong>SQL</strong> queries, mapping workflows, or auditing data consistency, I spend my spare time on my terrace in Gurugram growing mushrooms and automating personal workflows with <strong>n8n</strong>. Cultivating mushrooms in North India's climate is an exercise in strict variable control\u2014if humidity, airflow, or substrate prep drifts even slightly, the batch fails. I bring that exact same practical stewardship to enterprise systems, whether I am managing <strong>data integrity and error resolution</strong>, configuring system frameworks, or ensuring meticulous accuracy in daily operations.</p>", "para3_impact_story_html": "<p>Furthermore, I believe data management is only as useful as the operational alignment it drives. During my time at Concentrix, our workforce data kept flagging quality drops in new training cohorts, and simply sending leadership another dashboard wasn\u2019t solving it. I dug into the recruitment funnel, traced the disconnect between screening and floor realities, and successfully advocated to embed our training team directly into the hiring workflow\u2014a structural shift that drove an <strong>84% improvement in hire quality</strong>. I apply that same cross-functional problem-solving today at Highspring India, partnering across <strong>4+ engineering and business groups</strong> to cut manual reporting overhead by 40% and resolve hundreds of data consistency gaps.</p>", "para4_resilience_html": "<p>While my technical foundation across SQL, Python, and data governance is robust, I understand that adapting to proprietary airline and catering management architectures requires a steep learning curve on day one. Early in my career, navigating real-world constraints taught me how to strip away noise, focus on fundamentals, and become a <strong>dedicated learner with a sharp focus</strong> on operational excellence. Above all, I am <strong>unconditionally dependable</strong>\u2014when I take ownership of a system or dataset, you will never have to chase me to see it through.</p>", "para5_closing_html": "<p>I would value the chance to bring this grounded ownership, rigorous attention to detail, and steady execution to your team at United.</p><p>Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to discussing how my experience can support your upcoming data and systems initiatives.</p>"}, "index": 10, "role": "Analyst - Catering Systems Administrator", "category": "operations_strategy", "jobUrl": "https://careers.united.com/us/en/c/corporate-jobs", "jdSnippet": "Description\nJob Overview and Responsibilities\n\nThe Analyst - Catering Systems Administrator plays a critical role in maintaining the integrity and accuracy of catering data across United\u2019s systems and tools. This position supports business partners in delivering seamless catering services for flights systemwide through meticulous data management, system administration, and process optimization.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n\u2022 Data Management & Quality Assurance: Enter, verify, and maintain accurate catering data in United\u2019s management systems, ensuring timely updates with the precision required to support operational excellence\n\n\u2022 System Architecture & Configuration: Design and build system framework and codes to optimize service scheduling and ensure accurate vendor payments across the catering network\n\n\u2022 Data Integrity & Error Resolution: Conduct comprehensive data audits, identify inconsistencies, and collaborate with stakeholders to resolve issues while maintaining the highest standards of data quality\n\n\u2022 Technical Issue Resolution: Serve as a liaison between internal and external stakeholders to report, monitor, and resolve technical challenges efficiently\n\n\u2022 Process Improvement: Develop and implement scalable process enhancements that drive operational efficiency and organizational agility\n\n\u2022 Systems Administration: Oversee system setup, maintenance, vendor access management, and corporate compliance requirements\n\n\u2022 Cross-Functional Collaboration: Partner with diverse teams and external vendors to support ad-hoc projects and ensure operational accuracy\n\n \n\nThis position is offered on local terms and conditions.  Expatriate assignments and sponsorship for employment visas, even on a time-limited visa status, will not be awarded. This position is for United Airlines Business Services Pvt. Ltd - a wholly owned subsidiary of United Airlines Inc.\n\n \n\nQualifications\nQualifications\n\nRequired Qualifications:\n\n\u2022 Bachelor\u2019s degree in Hospitality, Business Administration, or related field\n\n\u2022 3+ years of experience in data entry and administrative support for large-scale teams and systems\n\n\u2022 Exceptional attention to detail and accuracy\n\n\u2022 Strong analytical and data management capabilities\n\n\u2022 Proven ability to work effectively across multiple stakeholder groups\n\n\u2022 Self-motivated with the ability to work independently in a remote environment\n\n\u2022 Excellent written and verbal communication skills\n\n\u2022 Solution-oriented mindset with strong problem-solving abilities\n\n\u2022 Legal authorization to work in India without sponsorship requirements\n\n\u2022 Fluency in English (written and spoken)\n\n\u2022 Ability to lead projects\n\nPreferred Qualifications:\n\n\u2022 Advanced degree or specialization in Hospitality, Catering/Food Services, or Airline Industry\n\n\u00b7  Experience using AI tools like Copilot, Gemini etc.\n\n\u2022 Technical proficiency in SQL and Python\n\n\u2022 Knowledge of airport or airline catering operations\n\n\u2022 Experience with continuous improvement methodologies\n\n\u2022 Familiarity with enterprise management systems (Oracle, CAE, Coupa, SAP, etc.)", "lastUpdate": "2026-10-07 15:15 IST", "referralName": "", "referralContact": "", "referralStatus": "", "resumeFileId": "1cZCb1EHf82miILMVWTs6AKs9hgxClrGm", "resumeUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clFileId": "1w2tObZiTq_cVcexsvJh3fwrAY_3mNDYV", "clUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "sections": {"summary": "<p>Senior Data &amp; Business Analyst combining extensive enterprise data analytics and operations intelligence experience with a strong foundation in commercial strategy and stakeholder consulting. Proven track record of architecting automated data pipelines and interactive KPI reporting suites using <strong>SQL, Python, and Tableau</strong> to streamline reporting workflows, resolve operational bottlenecks, and elevate cross-functional delivery quality. Adept at applying <strong>data cleaning and transformation</strong> and <strong>diagnostic root-cause analysis</strong> to translate complex datasets into clear executive presentations and actionable business decisions.</p>", "skills_html": "<ul>\n  <li><strong>Data Analysis &amp; Database Management:</strong> SQL (Postgresql, Mysql, Bigquery), Python (Pandas, Numpy), Excel, Api/data Integration, Database Management, R, Jupyter Notebooks</li>\n  <li><strong>Business Intelligence &amp; Visualization:</strong> Dashboard/report Automation, KPI Scorecard Design, Tableau, Interactive Dashboards, Executive Presentations, Narrative Insight Synthesis</li>\n  <li><strong>Data Governance &amp; Process Optimization:</strong> Quality Assurance, Data Cleaning &amp; Wrangling, Data Transformation, Identifying Improvement Opportunities, Automating Workflows (n8n), Root-cause &amp; Variance Analysis</li>\n  <li><strong>Stakeholder Collaboration &amp; Strategy:</strong> Critical Thinking &amp; Problem Solving, Stakeholder Communication, Cross-functional Teamwork, Business Acumen, Consulting &amp; Client Engagement, Training &amp; Mentorship</li>\n</ul>", "exp1_bullets": "<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Sr. Data Analyst, Highspring India \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Oct 2025 - Present</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Spearheaded end-to-end <strong>SQL data modelling</strong> and pipeline optimization across 1M+ monthly records using Python and BigQuery, cutting manual reporting overhead by 40%.</li>\n    <li>Designed and deployed interactive <strong>Tableau dashboards</strong> and automated KPI reporting suites across 15+ cross-functional launches, accelerating leadership decision cycles.</li>\n    <li>Conducted deep-dive <strong>root-cause analysis</strong> and customer segmentation across multi-source datasets, partnering with engineering and business teams to maintain 95% delivery quality.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Lead Trainer, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>April 2022 \u2013 Aug 2025</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Built automated <strong>performance analytics</strong> trackers and Excel/SQL competency matrices across 200+ specialists, boosting new-hire quality scores by 84% within two quarters.</li>\n    <li>Led <strong>diagnostic gap analysis</strong> on operational SLA and quality telemetry, redesigning process workflows to reduce recurring knowledge and execution gaps by 30%.</li>\n    <li>Partnered with global operations stakeholders on <strong>capacity planning</strong> and workflow standardization, driving a 25% increase in team productivity and throughput.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Customer Support Representative, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Jan 2021 \u2013 Mar 2022</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Resolved escalated consumer inquiries by utilizing <strong>CRM telemetry</strong> and historical performance metrics, accelerating ticket resolution speed by 35% across high-volume queues.</li>\n    <li>Analyzed user interaction trends to identify recurring <strong>service bottlenecks</strong>, partnering with operations leads to streamline workflows and boost customer satisfaction.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Founder | Creative Director, Maerke Stratcomm \u2013 New Delhi, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>June 2010 \u2013 July 2020</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Directed <strong>commercial analytics</strong>, pricing strategy, and market segmentation for 15+ B2B and retail clients, driving a 30% increase in customer acquisition.</li>\n    <li>Implemented <strong>funnel performance tracking</strong> and ROI attribution models across regional distribution channels, expanding HORECA and enterprise account revenue by 25%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>", "exp2_bullets": "", "exp3_bullets": ""}, "clHtml": "<p class=\"salutation\"><strong>To the Hiring Team at United,</strong></p>\n<p>What caught my attention about the <strong>Analyst - Catering Systems Administrator</strong> role at United is how directly it addresses the behind-the-scenes precision required to keep a massive operational network moving. Ensuring accurate data, vendor payments, and seamless system configurations across flight catering requires an analytical eye that respects how small data errors compound at scale. Having spent the last several years turning messy operational workflows into clean data models and structured BI\u2014preceded by a decade running my own commercial operations and B2B sales\u2014I know that logistical reliability lives or dies in the details of the database.</p>\n<p>When I am not writing <strong>SQL</strong> queries, mapping workflows, or auditing data consistency, I spend my spare time on my terrace in Gurugram growing mushrooms and automating personal workflows with <strong>n8n</strong>. Cultivating mushrooms in North India's climate is an exercise in strict variable control\u2014if humidity, airflow, or substrate prep drifts even slightly, the batch fails. I bring that exact same practical stewardship to enterprise systems, whether I am managing <strong>data integrity and error resolution</strong>, configuring system frameworks, or ensuring meticulous accuracy in daily operations.</p>\n<p>Furthermore, I believe data management is only as useful as the operational alignment it drives. During my time at Concentrix, our workforce data kept flagging quality drops in new training cohorts, and simply sending leadership another dashboard wasn\u2019t solving it. I dug into the recruitment funnel, traced the disconnect between screening and floor realities, and successfully advocated to embed our training team directly into the hiring workflow\u2014a structural shift that drove an <strong>84% improvement in hire quality</strong>. I apply that same cross-functional problem-solving today at Highspring India, partnering across <strong>4+ engineering and business groups</strong> to cut manual reporting overhead by 40% and resolve hundreds of data consistency gaps.</p>\n<p>While my technical foundation across SQL, Python, and data governance is robust, I understand that adapting to proprietary airline and catering management architectures requires a steep learning curve on day one. Early in my career, navigating real-world constraints taught me how to strip away noise, focus on fundamentals, and become a <strong>dedicated learner with a sharp focus</strong> on operational excellence. Above all, I am <strong>unconditionally dependable</strong>\u2014when I take ownership of a system or dataset, you will never have to chase me to see it through.</p>\n<p>I would value the chance to bring this grounded ownership, rigorous attention to detail, and steady execution to your team at United.</p><p>Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to discussing how my experience can support your upcoming data and systems initiatives.</p>"}, {"sNo": "11", "sNoNum": 11, "resumeId": "RES-11", "company": "University of Phoenix", "industry": "University", "jobId": "7531", "title": "Student Account Analyst", "jd": "About the Position\n\n\nThe Student Account Analyst performs financial and operational research and account analyses of student accounts to ensure students\u2019 billing invoices align with the terms and provisions of any enrollment, tuition assistance or other agreements that affect students\u2019 invoices.  Additionally, an individual audits various reports to ensure compliance with University policies and regulatory guidelines. A Student Account Analyst prepares daily accounting reconciliations, processes payments and refunds, and prepares various accounting transactions in accordance with University policy and generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP).\n\n What You\u2019ll Do:\nProduce routine and/or ad-hoc reports, using data extraction techniques, to audit student accounts and identify any required adjustments, including verification and application of tuition reduction benefits when applicable.  Identify discrepancies and perform necessary research/analysis to determine appropriate resolution. Ensure timely, accurate and compliant daily reconciliation of all accounts. \nAnalyze account information to calculate correct charges, adjustments and/or refunds in alignment with University policy, Master Service Agreement conditions, and applicable regulations.  Prepare related accounting transactions and ensure timely and accurate completion on a daily basis.\nManage payment receipt via lockbox management, ACH and wire transactions, Collection Agency payments, credit card transactions, and bank reconciliations.\nInterpret government documents and provide clarification to internal and external entities.\nCreate and/or update standard operating procedures in accordance with University policies, GAAP, Sarbanes-Oxley and/or other regulatory/compliance requirements, as applicable.\nSupport Tribal Accounts and Workforce Solutions.\nProvide support to internal and external stakeholders.\nPerform other duties as assigned or apparent.\nNOTE:  The Primary Accountabilities above are intended to describe the general content and requirements of the position and are not intended to be an exhaustive statement of duties.  Incumbents may perform all or most of the Primary Accountabilities listed above.  Specific goals or responsibilities will be documented in incumbents\u2019 performance objectives as outlined by the incumbents\u2019 immediate manager.\n\nSupervisory Duties: None\n\n#LI-Remote\n\nWhat You Bring to the Table\n\n\nMinimum education and related work experience:\n\n\u2022 High School Diploma or GED\n\n\u2022 One (1) year of experience in a role, such as accounts payable/receivable, that required knowledge and use of basic accounting skills and analysis\n\nAdditional Qualifications: \n\n\u2022 Bachelor\u2019s degree in finance, accounting, or related field \n\n\u2022 Two (2) years of general accounting experience \n\n\u2022 Knowledge of financial / accounting concepts (GAAP)\n\n\u2022 Strong Excel skills, including a working knowledge of an array of Excel formulas, as well as working knowledge of a variety of financial software/platforms, such as Oracle Financials, Oracle Vocado, Salesforce, MS Teams, SharePoint\n\n\u2022 Experience with SQL and Dataload \n\n\u2022 Able to research and analyze data and draw conclusions\n\n\u2022 Good time management and prioritization attributes\n\n\u2022 Effective written and verbal communication skills to communicate with internal and external customers via a variety of communication channels\n\n\u2022 Understanding of and able to communicate using standard financial terms\n\n\u2022 Able to successfully work in a very time sensitive role with a high degree of accuracy to ensure compliance and regulatory deadlines must be met\n\n\u2022 Possess high work standards and attention to detail\n\n\u2022 Comfortable working in a fast-paced environment\n\n\u2022 Demonstrate professionalism, accountability, customer/client focus, and teamwork\n\nUniversity of Phoenix is an Equal Opportunity employer. \n\n\nIf you are an active-duty military member seeking employment when off-duty, compliance with Department of Defense Joint Ethics Regulation, 5500-7-R, is required prior to starting employment with University of Phoenix. You are advised to contact your base Judge Advocate General to seek such approval and answer any questions.\nPay Range\n\nThe hourly pay rate range is $19.33 (minimum), $26.97 (midpoint), and $34.62 (maximum). The annualized amount, not including eligible overtime pay, is $40,200 (minimum), $56,100 (midpoint), and $72,000 (maximum).*\n*Typical hiring range is between the minimum and midpoint of the above pay range. Actual starting base pay may vary based on factors such as education, experience, skills, location and budget. Compensation above the midpoint is generally associated with experienced, long-tenured employees who have demonstrated sustained performance and expertise in the role.\n\nYour work is critical to helping adult learners achieve their dreams, and we\u2019re committed to rewarding you for your efforts. We offer a competitive, comprehensive total rewards package designed to help you achieve your health, financial, educational and work-life balance goals.\n \nFull-time employees are eligible for:\nMedical, dental and vision plans; Flexible Spending Accounts; Health Savings Accounts; Life and Disability insurance; and our Wellness incentive program;\nCompetitive 401(k) employer match;\nSubstantial tuition discount for you and eligible dependents; and,\nA generous time off package, including paid vacation, sick time and company holidays.*", "location": "US-AZ - Phoenix (Remote)", "portal": "Company site", "jdUrl": "https://uop.avature.net/careers/SearchJobs", "status": "Applied", "stageBucket": "Applied", "resumeStatus": "Ready for Review", "clStatus": "Ready for Review", "combinedDocStatus": "To be reviewed", "appliedOn": "8/25/2026", "followUpDate": "", "createdOn": "8/25/2026 09:00 IST", "lastUpdated": "2026-10-07 15:15 IST", "reference": "", "hrName": "", "hrEmail": "", "hrPhone": "", "reviewerNotes": "", "clNotes": "", "generalNotes": "", "aboutCompany": "Online and campus higher education institution.", "resumeDriveId": "1PDWuVG3wILVLrgAPjR6dm91s8TIfxeRZ", "resumeLink": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "resumePreviewUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clDriveId": "", "clLink": "https://docs.google.com/document/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DOCUMENT_ID/edit", "clPreviewUrl": "", "roleCategory": "finance_fpa_analyst", "extract