>service bottlenecks</strong>, partnering with operations leads to streamline workflows and boost customer satisfaction.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Founder | Creative Director, Maerke Stratcomm \u2013 New Delhi, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>June 2010 \u2013 July 2020</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Directed <strong>commercial analytics</strong>, pricing strategy, and market segmentation for 15+ B2B and retail clients, driving a 30% increase in customer acquisition.</li>\n    <li>Implemented <strong>funnel performance tracking</strong> and ROI attribution models across regional distribution channels, expanding HORECA and enterprise account revenue by 25%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>", "certifications_html": "<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Tableau Business Intelligence Analyst Professional Certificate</span><span class=\"cert-date\">May 2025</span></div>\n<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Google Advanced Data Analytics</span><span class=\"cert-date\">In Progress</span></div>\n<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Google Project Management</span><span class=\"cert-date\">In Progress</span></div>", "education_html": "<div class=\"edu-row\"><span>University of Delhi, B.Comm(Hons.)</span><span class=\"edu-date\">2013 \u2013 2016</span></div>", "hobbies_html": "<div class=\"hobbies-line\">Practicing Buddhism &nbsp;|&nbsp; Automating life with n8n &nbsp;|&nbsp; Growing Mushrooms</div>"}, "clSections": {"hasStoredCl": false, "salutation_html": "<p class=\"salutation\">Dear Hiring Manager at University of Phoenix,</p>", "para1_hook_html": "<p>I am writing to apply for the Student Account Analyst role at University of Phoenix. With over five years of hands-on experience building reliable SQL and Python reporting pipelines, designing executive Tableau dashboards, and partnering with product and operations leaders, I am eager to contribute immediately to University of Phoenix's data and analytics goals.</p>", "para2_stewardship_html": "<p>Throughout my career across high-volume operational and business intelligence environments, I have focused on turning complex, fragmented datasets into clear, trustworthy decision frameworks. Whether automating recurring ETL workflows or establishing governed KPI definitions across teams, I prioritize data accuracy and practical business impact.</p>", "para3_impact_story_html": "<p>In my recent work, I re-engineered manual reporting workflows into automated SQL and Tableau pipelines that reduced reporting latency by over 40% while uncovering key drivers of funnel conversion and SLA performance. This blend of technical execution and stakeholder communication aligns closely with what University of Phoenix seeks in this position.</p>", "para4_resilience_html": "<p>I thrive in fast-paced environments where requirements evolve quickly and cross-functional clarity is essential. My background spans end-to-end requirement gathering, UAT governance, root-cause diagnostics, and translating technical findings for non-technical leadership.</p>", "para5_closing_html": "<p>Thank you for your time and consideration. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my background in SQL, Python, Tableau, and business analysis can support University of Phoenix's upcoming initiatives.</p>"}, "index": 11, "role": "Student Account Analyst", "category": "finance_fpa_analyst", "jobUrl": "https://uop.avature.net/careers/SearchJobs", "jdSnippet": "About the Position\n\n\nThe Student Account Analyst performs financial and operational research and account analyses of student accounts to ensure students\u2019 billing invoices align with the terms and provisions of any enrollment, tuition assistance or other agreements that affect students\u2019 invoices.  Additionally, an individual audits various reports to ensure compliance with University policies and regulatory guidelines. A Student Account Analyst prepares daily accounting reconciliations, processes payments and refunds, and prepares various accounting transactions in accordance with University policy and generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP).\n\n What You\u2019ll Do:\nProduce routine and/or ad-hoc reports, using data extraction techniques, to audit student accounts and identify any required adjustments, including verification and application of tuition reduction benefits when applicable.  Identify discrepancies and perform necessary research/analysis to determine appropriate resolution. Ensure timely, accurate and compliant daily reconciliation of all accounts. \nAnalyze account information to calculate correct charges, adjustments and/or refunds in alignment with University policy, Master Service Agreement conditions, and applicable regulations.  Prepare related accounting transactions and ensure timely and accurate completion on a daily basis.\nManage payment receipt via lockbox management, ACH and wire transactions, Collection Agency payments, credit card transactions, and bank reconciliations.\nInterpret government documents and provide clarification to internal and external entities.\nCreate and/or update standard operating procedures in accordance with University policies, GAAP, Sarbanes-Oxley and/or other regulatory/compliance requirements, as applicable.\nSupport Tribal Accounts and Workforce Solutions.\nProvide support to internal and external stakeholders.\nPerform other duties as assigned or apparent.\nNOTE:  The Primary Accountabilities above are intended to describe the general content and requirements of the position and are not intended to be an exhaustive statement of duties.  Incumbents may perform all or most of the Primary Accountabilities listed above.  Specific goals or responsibilities will be documented in incumbents\u2019 performance objectives as outlined by the incumbents\u2019 immediate manager.\n\nSupervisory Duties: None\n\n#LI-Remote\n\nWhat You Bring to the Table\n\n\nMinimum education and related work experience:\n\n\u2022 High School Diploma or GED\n\n\u2022 One (1) year of experience in a role, such as accounts payable/receivable, that required knowledge and use of basic accounting skills and analysis\n\nAdditional Qualifications: \n\n\u2022 Bachelor\u2019s degree in finance, accounting, or related field \n\n\u2022 Two (2) years of general accounting experience \n\n\u2022 Knowledge of financial / accounting concepts (GAAP)\n\n\u2022 Strong Excel skills, including a working knowledge of an array of Excel formulas, as well as working knowledge of a variety of financial software/platforms, such as Oracle Financials, Oracle Vocado, Salesforce, MS Teams, SharePoint\n\n\u2022 Experience with SQL and Dataload \n\n\u2022 Able to research and analyze data and draw conclusions\n\n\u2022 Good time management and prioritization attributes\n\n\u2022 Effective written and verbal communication skills to communicate with internal and external customers via a variety of communication channels\n\n\u2022 Understanding of and able to communicate using standard financial terms\n\n\u2022 Able to successfully work in a very time sensitive role with a high degree of accuracy to ensure compliance and regulatory deadlines must be met\n\n\u2022 Possess high work standards and attention to detail\n\n\u2022 Comfortable working in a fast-paced environment\n\n\u2022 Demonstrate professionalism, accountability, customer/client focus, and teamwork\n\nUniversity of Phoenix is an Equal Opportunity employer. \n\n\nIf you are an active-duty military member seeking employment when off-duty, compliance with Department of Defense Joint Ethics Regulation, 5500-7-R, is required prior to starting employment with University of Phoenix. You are advised to contact your base Judge Advocate General to seek such approval and answer any questions.\nPay Range\n\nThe hourly pay rate range is $19.33 (minimum), $26.97 (midpoint), and $34.62 (maximum). The annualized amount, not including eligible overtime pay, is $40,200 (minimum), $56,100 (midpoint), and $72,000 (maximum).*\n*Typical hiring range is between the minimum and midpoint of the above pay range. Actual starting base pay may vary based on factors such as education, experience, skills, location and budget. Compensation above the midpoint is generally associated with experienced, long-tenured employees who have demonstrated sustained performance and expertise in the role.\n\nYour work is critical to helping adult learners achieve their dreams, and we\u2019re committed to rewarding you for your efforts. We offer a competitive, comprehensive total rewards package designed to help you achieve your health, financial, educational and work-life balance goals.\n \nFull-time employees are eligible for:\nMedical, dental and vision plans; Flexible Spending Accounts; Health Savings Accounts; Life and Disability insurance; and our Wellness incentive program;\nCompetitive 401(k) employer match;\nSubstantial tuition discount for you and eligible dependents; and,\nA generous time off package, including paid vacation, sick time and company holidays.*", "lastUpdate": "2026-10-07 15:15 IST", "referralName": "", "referralContact": "", "referralStatus": "", "resumeFileId": "1PDWuVG3wILVLrgAPjR6dm91s8TIfxeRZ", "resumeUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clFileId": "", "clUrl": "https://docs.google.com/document/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DOCUMENT_ID/edit", "sections": {"summary": "<p>Senior Data &amp; Business Analyst combining extensive enterprise data analytics and operations intelligence experience with a strong foundation in commercial strategy and stakeholder consulting. Proven track record of architecting automated data pipelines and interactive KPI reporting suites using <strong>SQL, Python, and Tableau</strong> to streamline reporting workflows, resolve operational bottlenecks, and elevate cross-functional delivery quality. Adept at applying <strong>data cleaning and transformation</strong> and <strong>diagnostic root-cause analysis</strong> to translate complex datasets into clear executive presentations and actionable business decisions.</p>", "skills_html": "<ul>\n  <li><strong>Data Analysis &amp; Database Management:</strong> SQL (Postgresql, Mysql, Bigquery), Excel, Api/data Integration, Database Management, Python (Pandas, Numpy), R, Jupyter Notebooks</li>\n  <li><strong>Business Intelligence &amp; Visualization:</strong> Dashboard/report Automation, KPI Scorecard Design, Tableau, Interactive Dashboards, Executive Presentations, Narrative Insight Synthesis</li>\n  <li><strong>Data Governance &amp; Process Optimization:</strong> Data Cleaning &amp; Wrangling, Data Transformation, Root-cause &amp; Variance Analysis, Quality Assurance, Automating Workflows (n8n), Identifying Improvement Opportunities</li>\n  <li><strong>Stakeholder Collaboration &amp; Strategy:</strong> Stakeholder Communication, Cross-functional Teamwork, Consulting &amp; Client Engagement, Critical Thinking &amp; Problem Solving, Training &amp; Mentorship, Business Acumen</li>\n</ul>", "exp1_bullets": "<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Sr. Data Analyst, Highspring India \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Oct 2025 - Present</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Spearheaded end-to-end <strong>data profiling and reconciliation</strong> across 1M+ monthly records using SQL and Python, resolving reporting discrepancies and cutting manual overhead by 40%.</li>\n    <li>Designed and deployed interactive <strong>Tableau dashboards</strong> and automated KPI reporting suites across 15+ cross-functional launches, accelerating leadership decision cycles.</li>\n    <li>Conducted deep-dive <strong>root-cause analysis</strong> and customer segmentation across multi-source datasets, partnering with engineering and business teams to maintain 95% delivery quality.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Lead Trainer, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>April 2022 \u2013 Aug 2025</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Built automated <strong>performance analytics</strong> trackers and Excel/SQL competency matrices across 200+ specialists, boosting new-hire quality scores by 84% within two quarters.</li>\n    <li>Led <strong>diagnostic gap analysis</strong> on operational SLA and quality telemetry, redesigning process workflows to reduce recurring knowledge and execution gaps by 30%.</li>\n    <li>Partnered with global operations stakeholders on <strong>capacity planning</strong> and workflow standardization, driving a 25% increase in team productivity and throughput.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Customer Support Representative, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Jan 2021 \u2013 Mar 2022</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Resolved escalated consumer inquiries by utilizing <strong>CRM telemetry</strong> and historical performance metrics, accelerating ticket resolution speed by 35% across high-volume queues.</li>\n    <li>Analyzed user interaction trends to identify recurring <strong>service bottlenecks</strong>, partnering with operations leads to streamline workflows and boost customer satisfaction.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Founder | Creative Director, Maerke Stratcomm \u2013 New Delhi, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>June 2010 \u2013 July 2020</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Directed <strong>commercial analytics</strong>, pricing strategy, and market segmentation for 15+ B2B and retail clients, driving a 30% increase in customer acquisition.</li>\n    <li>Implemented <strong>funnel performance tracking</strong> and ROI attribution models across regional distribution channels, expanding HORECA and enterprise account revenue by 25%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>", "exp2_bullets": "", "exp3_bullets": ""}, "clHtml": "<p class=\"salutation\">Dear Hiring Manager at University of Phoenix,</p>\n<p>I am writing to apply for the Student Account Analyst role at University of Phoenix. With over five years of hands-on experience building reliable SQL and Python reporting pipelines, designing executive Tableau dashboards, and partnering with product and operations leaders, I am eager to contribute immediately to University of Phoenix's data and analytics goals.</p>\n<p>Throughout my career across high-volume operational and business intelligence environments, I have focused on turning complex, fragmented datasets into clear, trustworthy decision frameworks. Whether automating recurring ETL workflows or establishing governed KPI definitions across teams, I prioritize data accuracy and practical business impact.</p>\n<p>In my recent work, I re-engineered manual reporting workflows into automated SQL and Tableau pipelines that reduced reporting latency by over 40% while uncovering key drivers of funnel conversion and SLA performance. This blend of technical execution and stakeholder communication aligns closely with what University of Phoenix seeks in this position.</p>\n<p>I thrive in fast-paced environments where requirements evolve quickly and cross-functional clarity is essential. My background spans end-to-end requirement gathering, UAT governance, root-cause diagnostics, and translating technical findings for non-technical leadership.</p>\n<p>Thank you for your time and consideration. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my background in SQL, Python, Tableau, and business analysis can support University of Phoenix's upcoming initiatives.</p>"}, {"sNo": "12", "sNoNum": 12, "resumeId": "c9018fde-3581-414f-92a4-e654615a78b0", "company": "United", "industry": "Airlines", "jobId": "GGN00002617", "title": "Analyst - Predictive Safety Analytics", "jd": "Description\nCorporate safety is integral for ensuring a safe workplace for our employees and travel experience for our customers. This role is responsible for supporting the development and implementation of a cohesive safety data strategy and supporting the Director of Safety Management Systems (SMS) in growing United\u2019s Corporate Safety predictive analytics capabilities.\n\nThis analyst will serve as a subject matter expert for corporate safety data analytics and predictive insight strategy and execution. This position will be responsible for supporting new efforts to deliver insightful data analysis and build new key metrics for use by the entire United Safety organization, with the goal of enabling data driven decision making and understanding for corporate safety. The analyst will be responsible for becoming the subject matter expert in several corporate safety specific data streams and leveraging this expertise to deliver insights which are actionable and allow for a predictive approach to safety risk mitigation.\n\nDevelop and implement predictive/prescriptive data analytics workflows for Safety Data Management and streamlining processes\nCollaborate with Digital Technology and United Operational teams to analyze, predict and reduce safety risks and provide measurable solutions\nSupport United\u2019s Safety Management System (SMS) with predictive data analytics by designing and developing statistical models\nAreas of focus will include, but are not limited to:\nPredictive and prescriptive analytics\nTrain and validate models\nCreation and maintenance of standardized corporate safety performance metrics\nImplementation of new data pipelines\nDelivery of prescriptive analysis insights to internal stakeholders\nJob Responsibilities:\n\nCreate and manage new methods for data analysis that provide prescriptive and predictive insights on corporate safety data, leveraging AI tools such as Microsoft Copilot, ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude, and Perplexity to improve analytical efficiency and support data-driven decision-making.\nDesign and maintain new and existing corporate safety data pipelines and analytical workflows.\nPartner with US and India based internal partners to establish new data analysis workflows and provide analytical support to corporate and divisional work groups.\nCollaborate with corporate and divisional safety partners to ensure standardization and consistency between all safety analytics efforts enterprise wide.\nProvide support and ongoing subject matter expertise regarding a set of high priority corporate safety datasets and ongoing analytics efforts on those datasets.\nProvide tracking and status update reporting on ongoing assignments, projects, and efforts to US and India based leaders.\nThis position is offered on local terms and conditions.  Expatriate assignments and sponsorship for employment visas, even on a time-limited visa status, will not be awarded. This position is for United Airlines Business Services Pvt. Ltd - a wholly owned subsidiary of United Airlines Inc.\n\nQualifications\nWhat\u2019s needed to succeed (Minimum Qualifications):\n\nBachelor's degree or 4 years of relevant work experience\nBachelor's degree in computer science, data science, information sytems, engineering, or another quantitative field (i.e. mathematics, statistics, economics, etc.)\n2+ years experience in data analytics, statistics , experience in predictive modeling, NLP, ML, Gen AI\nIntermediate level SQL skills\nExperience with Python\nProficiency writing complex code using both traditional and modern technologies/languages (i.e. Python, Tableau etc.) for queries, procedures, and analytic processing to create useable data insight\nStrong project management and communication skills\n2-3 years working with complex data (data analytics, information science, data visualization or other relevant quantitative field)\nHands-on experience using AI tools in projects, internships, or work environments.\nKnowledge of automation platforms such as Power Automate, Copilot Studio, Zapier, or n8n.", "location": "Gurugram, Haryana, India", "portal": "Company site", "jdUrl": "https://careers.united.com/us/en/c/corporate-jobs", "status": "Applied", "stageBucket": "Applied", "resumeStatus": "Ready for Review", "clStatus": "Ready for Review", "combinedDocStatus": "To be reviewed", "appliedOn": "9/2/2026", "followUpDate": "", "createdOn": "9/2/2026 09:00 IST", "lastUpdated": "2026-10-06 09:00 IST", "reference": "", "hrName": "", "hrEmail": "", "hrPhone": "", "reviewerNotes": "", "clNotes": "", "generalNotes": "", "aboutCompany": "Major global airline operating Digital Technology & Analytics center in Gurugram.", "resumeDriveId": "1XFFSZjGi9uwPNr5BBMbFXOJIKAzGFHUd", "resumeLink": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "resumePreviewUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clDriveId": "1bHgUsmex83N_2_GtNv4ZdTFW63WEJWu4", "clLink": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clPreviewUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "roleCategory": "Data & Business Analytics", "extractedKeywords": "", "revisionCount": 1, "clRevisionCount": 1, "resumeSections": {"summary_html": "<p>Senior Data &amp; Business Analyst combining extensive enterprise data analytics and operations intelligence experience with a strong foundation in commercial strategy and stakeholder consulting. Proven track record of leveraging <strong>SQL, Python, and Tableau</strong> for financial reconciliation, commercial pricing analysis, and automated KPI governance across enterprise and regional operations. Adept at applying <strong>data cleaning and transformation</strong> and <strong>funnel and cohort segmentation</strong> to translate complex datasets into clear executive presentations and actionable business decisions.</p>", "skills_html": "<ul><li><strong>Data Analysis &amp; Database Management:</strong> SQL (PostgreSQL, MySQL, BigQuery), Python (Pandas, NumPy), R, Excel, Jupyter Notebooks, API/Data Integration, Database Management</li><li><strong>Business Intelligence &amp; Visualization:</strong> KPI Scorecard Design, Tableau, Looker Studio, Dashboard/Report Automation, Interactive Dashboards, Executive Presentations</li><li><strong>Data Governance &amp; Process Optimization:</strong> Data Cleaning &amp; Wrangling, Data Transformation, Quality Assurance, Automating Workflows (n8n), Root-Cause &amp; Variance Analysis</li><li><strong>Stakeholder Collaboration &amp; Strategy:</strong> Cross-Functional Teamwork, Stakeholder Communication, Consulting &amp; Client Engagement, Training &amp; Mentorship, Business Acumen</li></ul>", "experience_html": "<div class=\"job-block\"><div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Sr. Data Analyst, Highspring India \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Oct 2025 - Present</strong></span></div><ul><li>Spearheaded end-to-end <strong>funnel and behavioral analytics</strong> across 1M+ monthly records using SQL and Python, uncovering conversion bottlenecks and cutting manual reporting overhead by 40%.</li><li>Designed and deployed interactive <strong>Tableau dashboards</strong> and automated KPI reporting suites across 15+ cross-functional launches, accelerating leadership decision cycles.</li><li>Conducted deep-dive <strong>root-cause analysis</strong> and customer segmentation across multi-source datasets, partnering with engineering and business teams to maintain 95% delivery quality.</li></ul></div><div class=\"job-block\"><div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Lead Trainer, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>April 2022 \u2013 Aug 2025</strong></span></div><ul><li>Built automated <strong>performance analytics</strong> trackers and Excel/SQL competency matrices across 200+ specialists, boosting new-hire quality scores by 84% within two quarters.</li><li>Led <strong>diagnostic gap analysis</strong> on operational SLA and quality telemetry, redesigning process workflows to reduce recurring knowledge and execution gaps by 30%.</li><li>Partnered with global operations stakeholders on <strong>capacity planning</strong> and workflow standardization, driving a 25% increase in team productivity and throughput.</li></ul></div><div class=\"job-block\"><div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Customer Support Representative, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Jan 2021 \u2013 Mar 2022</strong></span></div><ul><li>Resolved escalated consumer inquiries by utilizing <strong>CRM telemetry</strong> and historical performance metrics, accelerating ticket resolution speed by 35% across high-volume queues.</li><li>Analyzed user interaction trends to identify recurring <strong>service bottlenecks</strong>, partnering with operations leads to streamline workflows and boost customer satisfaction.</li></ul></div><div class=\"job-block\"><div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Founder | Creative Director, Maerke Stratcomm \u2013 New Delhi, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>June 2010 \u2013 July 2020</strong></span></div><ul><li>Directed <strong>commercial analytics</strong>, pricing strategy, and market segmentation for 15+ B2B and retail clients, driving a 30% increase in customer acquisition.</li><li>Implemented <strong>funnel performance tracking</strong> and ROI attribution models across regional distribution channels, expanding HORECA and enterprise account revenue by 25%.</li></ul></div>", "certifications_html": "<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Tableau Business Intelligence Analyst Professional Certificate</span><span class=\"cert-date\">May 2025</span></div><div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Google Advanced Data Analytics</span><span class=\"cert-date\">In Progress</span></div><div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Google Project Management</span><span class=\"cert-date\">In Progress</span></div>", "education_html": "<div class=\"edu-row\"><span>University of Delhi, B.Comm(Hons.)</span><span class=\"edu-date\">2013 \u2013 2016</span></div>", "hobbies_html": "<div class=\"hobbies-line\">Practicing Buddhism &nbsp;|&nbsp; Automating life with n8n &nbsp;|&nbsp; Growing Mushrooms</div>"}, "clSections": {"hasStoredCl": true, "salutation_html": "<div class=\"letter-meta\">\n  <div class=\"letter-date\">September 29, 2026</div>\n  <div class=\"recipient-block\">\n    <div>Hiring Team</div><div>United</div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"subject-line\"><strong>Subject: Application for the Analyst - Predictive Safety Analytics Role</strong></div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"salutation\">Dear Hiring Manager,</p>", "para1_hook_html": "<p>I am writing to apply for the Analyst - Predictive Safety Analytics role at United. What stood out to me in the job description is the focus on building predictive data workflows and turning safety data into clear insights. Before spending the last five years in data analytics, I ran my own small business for ten years. That mix taught me how much time teams lose when numbers do not match across different tools. Fixing those gaps between business teams and technical engineering is the part of the job I enjoy most.</p>", "para2_stewardship_html": "<p>Outside of writing SQL queries and building Tableau dashboards, I spend my free time on my terrace in Gurugram growing mushrooms and automating small daily tasks with n8n. Growing mushrooms in North India weather is not a fancy hobby. It comes down to watching basic details closely. If moisture or airflow slips even a little, the whole batch fails. I bring that same habit to my work when I check data quality, map workflows, or build safety reports that leaders rely on.</p>", "para3_impact_story_html": "<p>I also believe analysis is only useful when it solves a real problem on the ground. At Concentrix, our hiring data showed that new joiners were struggling once they started work. Sending another dashboard to management was not fixing the issue. I looked closely at the hiring steps and worked with leadership to bring our training team directly into the interview stage. That simple change improved hire quality by 84%. In my current role at Highspring India, I use the same practical approach across four engineering teams to automate recurring reports and cut manual work by 40%.</p>", "para4_resilience_html": "<p>My day-to-day work covers SQL, Python, Tableau, and working closely with business and tech teams. If the team at United uses an internal tool I have not worked with yet, I learn new systems quickly. Practical challenges early in my career taught me how to stay resourceful, focus on the basics, and get things done without hand-holding. When I take ownership of a task, nobody has to follow up twice.</p>", "para5_closing_html": "<p>I would welcome the chance to bring this steady, practical approach to United. Thank you for your time and consideration, and I look forward to speaking with you soon.</p>"}, "index": 12, "role": "Analyst - Predictive Safety Analytics", "category": "Data & Business Analytics", "jobUrl": "https://careers.united.com/us/en/c/corporate-jobs", "jdSnippet": "Description\nCorporate safety is integral for ensuring a safe workplace for our employees and travel experience for our customers. This role is responsible for supporting the development and implementation of a cohesive safety data strategy and supporting the Director of Safety Management Systems (SMS) in growing United\u2019s Corporate Safety predictive analytics capabilities.\n\nThis analyst will serve as a subject matter expert for corporate safety data analytics and predictive insight strategy and executi