tter expertise regarding a set of high priority corporate safety datasets and ongoing analytics efforts on those datasets.\nProvide tracking and status update reporting on ongoing assignments, projects, and efforts to US and India based leaders.\nThis position is offered on local terms and conditions.  Expatriate assignments and sponsorship for employment visas, even on a time-limited visa status, will not be awarded. This position is for United Airlines Business Services Pvt. Ltd - a wholly owned subsidiary of United Airlines Inc.\n\nQualifications\nWhat\u2019s needed to succeed (Minimum Qualifications):\n\nBachelor's degree or 4 years of relevant work experience\nBachelor's degree in computer science, data science, information sytems, engineering, or another quantitative field (i.e. mathematics, statistics, economics, etc.)\n2+ years experience in data analytics, statistics , experience in predictive modeling, NLP, ML, Gen AI\nIntermediate level SQL skills\nExperience with Python\nProficiency writing complex code using both traditional and modern technologies/languages (i.e. Python, Tableau etc.) for queries, procedures, and analytic processing to create useable data insight\nStrong project management and communication skills\n2-3 years working with complex data (data analytics, information science, data visualization or other relevant quantitative field)\nHands-on experience using AI tools in projects, internships, or work environments.\nKnowledge of automation platforms such as Power Automate, Copilot Studio, Zapier, or n8n.", "lastUpdate": "2026-10-06 09:00 IST", "referralName": "", "referralContact": "", "referralStatus": "", "resumeFileId": "1XFFSZjGi9uwPNr5BBMbFXOJIKAzGFHUd", "resumeUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clFileId": "1bHgUsmex83N_2_GtNv4ZdTFW63WEJWu4", "clUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "sections": {"summary": "<p>Senior Data &amp; Business Analyst combining extensive enterprise data analytics and operations intelligence experience with a strong foundation in commercial strategy and stakeholder consulting. Proven track record of leveraging <strong>SQL, Python, and Tableau</strong> for financial reconciliation, commercial pricing analysis, and automated KPI governance across enterprise and regional operations. Adept at applying <strong>data cleaning and transformation</strong> and <strong>funnel and cohort segmentation</strong> to translate complex datasets into clear executive presentations and actionable business decisions.</p>", "skills_html": "<ul><li><strong>Data Analysis &amp; Database Management:</strong> SQL (PostgreSQL, MySQL, BigQuery), Python (Pandas, NumPy), R, Excel, Jupyter Notebooks, API/Data Integration, Database Management</li><li><strong>Business Intelligence &amp; Visualization:</strong> KPI Scorecard Design, Tableau, Looker Studio, Dashboard/Report Automation, Interactive Dashboards, Executive Presentations</li><li><strong>Data Governance &amp; Process Optimization:</strong> Data Cleaning &amp; Wrangling, Data Transformation, Quality Assurance, Automating Workflows (n8n), Root-Cause &amp; Variance Analysis</li><li><strong>Stakeholder Collaboration &amp; Strategy:</strong> Cross-Functional Teamwork, Stakeholder Communication, Consulting &amp; Client Engagement, Training &amp; Mentorship, Business Acumen</li></ul>", "exp1_bullets": "<div class=\"job-block\"><div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Sr. Data Analyst, Highspring India \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Oct 2025 - Present</strong></span></div><ul><li>Spearheaded end-to-end <strong>funnel and behavioral analytics</strong> across 1M+ monthly records using SQL and Python, uncovering conversion bottlenecks and cutting manual reporting overhead by 40%.</li><li>Designed and deployed interactive <strong>Tableau dashboards</strong> and automated KPI reporting suites across 15+ cross-functional launches, accelerating leadership decision cycles.</li><li>Conducted deep-dive <strong>root-cause analysis</strong> and customer segmentation across multi-source datasets, partnering with engineering and business teams to maintain 95% delivery quality.</li></ul></div><div class=\"job-block\"><div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Lead Trainer, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>April 2022 \u2013 Aug 2025</strong></span></div><ul><li>Built automated <strong>performance analytics</strong> trackers and Excel/SQL competency matrices across 200+ specialists, boosting new-hire quality scores by 84% within two quarters.</li><li>Led <strong>diagnostic gap analysis</strong> on operational SLA and quality telemetry, redesigning process workflows to reduce recurring knowledge and execution gaps by 30%.</li><li>Partnered with global operations stakeholders on <strong>capacity planning</strong> and workflow standardization, driving a 25% increase in team productivity and throughput.</li></ul></div><div class=\"job-block\"><div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Customer Support Representative, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Jan 2021 \u2013 Mar 2022</strong></span></div><ul><li>Resolved escalated consumer inquiries by utilizing <strong>CRM telemetry</strong> and historical performance metrics, accelerating ticket resolution speed by 35% across high-volume queues.</li><li>Analyzed user interaction trends to identify recurring <strong>service bottlenecks</strong>, partnering with operations leads to streamline workflows and boost customer satisfaction.</li></ul></div><div class=\"job-block\"><div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Founder | Creative Director, Maerke Stratcomm \u2013 New Delhi, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>June 2010 \u2013 July 2020</strong></span></div><ul><li>Directed <strong>commercial analytics</strong>, pricing strategy, and market segmentation for 15+ B2B and retail clients, driving a 30% increase in customer acquisition.</li><li>Implemented <strong>funnel performance tracking</strong> and ROI attribution models across regional distribution channels, expanding HORECA and enterprise account revenue by 25%.</li></ul></div>", "exp2_bullets": "", "exp3_bullets": ""}, "clHtml": "<div class=\"letter-meta\">\n  <div class=\"letter-date\">September 29, 2026</div>\n  <div class=\"recipient-block\">\n    <div>Hiring Team</div><div>United</div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"subject-line\"><strong>Subject: Application for the Analyst - Predictive Safety Analytics Role</strong></div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"salutation\">Dear Hiring Manager,</p>\n<p>I am writing to apply for the Analyst - Predictive Safety Analytics role at United. What stood out to me in the job description is the focus on building predictive data workflows and turning safety data into clear insights. Before spending the last five years in data analytics, I ran my own small business for ten years. That mix taught me how much time teams lose when numbers do not match across different tools. Fixing those gaps between business teams and technical engineering is the part of the job I enjoy most.</p>\n<p>Outside of writing SQL queries and building Tableau dashboards, I spend my free time on my terrace in Gurugram growing mushrooms and automating small daily tasks with n8n. Growing mushrooms in North India weather is not a fancy hobby. It comes down to watching basic details closely. If moisture or airflow slips even a little, the whole batch fails. I bring that same habit to my work when I check data quality, map workflows, or build safety reports that leaders rely on.</p>\n<p>I also believe analysis is only useful when it solves a real problem on the ground. At Concentrix, our hiring data showed that new joiners were struggling once they started work. Sending another dashboard to management was not fixing the issue. I looked closely at the hiring steps and worked with leadership to bring our training team directly into the interview stage. That simple change improved hire quality by 84%. In my current role at Highspring India, I use the same practical approach across four engineering teams to automate recurring reports and cut manual work by 40%.</p>\n<p>My day-to-day work covers SQL, Python, Tableau, and working closely with business and tech teams. If the team at United uses an internal tool I have not worked with yet, I learn new systems quickly. Practical challenges early in my career taught me how to stay resourceful, focus on the basics, and get things done without hand-holding. When I take ownership of a task, nobody has to follow up twice.</p>\n<p>I would welcome the chance to bring this steady, practical approach to United. Thank you for your time and consideration, and I look forward to speaking with you soon.</p>"}, {"sNo": "13", "sNoNum": 13, "resumeId": "RES-13", "company": "Damco", "industry": "IT service", "jobId": "N/A", "title": "Business Analytics", "jd": "Job Summary:\nWe are looking for a strong analytics professional with expertise in Product Analytics, Business Analytics, or Data Analytics. The role will involve working with large-scale product and user data to understand user behavior, generate actionable insights, build scalable dashboards, and influence product and business decisions.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\nDesign, build, and maintain dashboards and reports using Tableau / Tableau.\nAnalyze product usage, feature adoption, funnels, cohorts, and business KPIs.\nConduct deep-dive and root-cause analysis to identify trends, anomalies, and performance drivers.\nDefine and evolve product success metrics and KPIs.\nPartner with Product Managers, Engineers, Product Marketing, GTM, and Finance teams.\nSupport product roadmap decisions, feature evaluation, launches, adoption, and business impact analysis.\nDesign and analyze A/B tests and experiments, inclu