ha Verma,</p>\n<p>I am writing to apply for the Business Analytics role at Damco. What stood out to me in the job description is the focus on turning user data into clear reports that guide product decisions. Before spending the last five years in data analytics, I ran my own small marketing agency for ten years. That mix taught me how much time teams lose when numbers do not match across different tools. Fixing those gaps between business teams and engineering is the part of the job I enjoy most.</p>\n<p>Outside of writing SQL queries and building Tableau dashboards, I spend my free time on my terrace in Gurugram growing mushrooms and automating small daily tasks with n8n. Growing mushrooms in North India weather is not a fancy hobby. It comes down to watching basic details closely. If moisture or airflow slips even a little, the whole batch fails. I bring that same habit to my work when I check data quality, map workflows, or build reports that leaders rely on.</p>\n<p>I also believe analysis is only useful when it solves a real problem on the ground. At Concentrix, our hiring data showed that new joiners were struggling once they started work. Sending another dashboard to management was not fixing the issue. I looked closely at the hiring steps and worked with leadership to bring our training team directly into the interview stage. That simple change improved hire quality by 84 percent. In my current role at Highspring India, I use the same practical approach across four engineering teams to automate recurring reports and cut manual work by 40 percent.</p>\n<p>My day-to-day work covers SQL, Python, Tableau, and working closely with business and tech teams. If your team uses an internal tool I have not worked with yet, I learn new systems quickly. Practical challenges early in my career taught me how to stay resourceful, focus on the basics, and get things done without hand-holding. When I take ownership of a task, you will not have to follow up twice.</p>\n<p>I would welcome the chance to bring this steady and practical approach to your team. Thank you for your time and consideration, and I look forward to speaking with you soon.</p>"}, {"sNo": "14", "sNoNum": 14, "resumeId": "RES-14", "company": "7-Eleven Global Solution Center", "industry": "IT service", "jobId": "10576", "title": "Data Analyst", "jd": "Role Summary:\n\nThe Analyst provides foundational analytics support across 7-Eleven\u2019s retail categories, enabling fact-based decisions for Merchandising and Category Management. This role is critical in building accurate reporting, validating data, and delivering baseline insights that fuel category growth and efficiency.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n\u00b7 Develop and maintain standardized reports/dashboards on sales, promotions, assortment, and vendor performance across categories.\n\n\u00b7 Ensure high-quality, accurate, and timely delivery of recurring reports and ad-hoc requests.\n\n\u00b7 Support pricing, promotion, and assortment analytics with initial insights and recommendations.\n\n\u00b7 Collaborate with senior team members to prepare inputs for category reviews and strategy decks.\n\n\u00b7 Maintain and improve data sources, trackers, and automation tools to drive efficiency.\n\nAttributes:\n\n\u00b7 Strong attention to detail with ability to validate and reconcile data across systems.\n\n\u00b7 Proficiency in Excel, SQL, and BI tools (Tableau preferred).\n\n\u00b7 Curiosity to learn the retail business model and eagerness to grow in analytics.", "location": "Bengaluru", "portal": "Company site", "jdUrl": "https://careers.7-eleven.com", "status": "Applied", "stageBucket": "Applied", "resumeStatus": "Approved & Learned", "clStatus": "Ready for Review", "combinedDocStatus": "LGTM", "appliedOn": "9/25/2026", "followUpDate": "9/28/2026", "createdOn": "9/25/2026 09:00 IST", "lastUpdated": "2026-10-06 09:00 IST", "reference": "", "hrName": "Kankona Roy", "hrEmail": "", "hrPhone": "", "reviewerNotes": "1. Remove 